the thousands digit from 4 to 5: 685,000.','The hundreds digit is 5, so round up the thousands digit from 4 to 5: 685,000.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(922,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: 45 + 15 × 4','Calculate: 45 + 15 × 4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"240\", \"105\", \"180\", \"120\"]','105','Apply BODMAS: Multiply first (15 × 4 = 60), then add 45 (45 + 60 = 105).','Apply BODMAS: Multiply first (15 × 4 = 60), then add 45 (45 + 60 = 105).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(923,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: (72 - 18) ÷ 6 + 12','Calculate: (72 - 18) ÷ 6 + 12','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"21\", \"24\", \"18\", \"15\"]','21','BODMAS: Brackets first (72 - 18 = 54), divide (54 ÷ 6 = 9), then add (9 + 12 = 21).','BODMAS: Brackets first (72 - 18 = 54), divide (54 ÷ 6 = 9), then add (9 + 12 = 21).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(924,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Which of the following is a prime number?','Which of the following is a prime number?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"49\", \"51\", \"53\", \"57\"]','53','53 has only two factors: 1 and 53. 49 = 7×7, 51 = 3×17, 57 = 3×19.','53 has only two factors: 1 and 53. 49 = 7×7, 51 = 3×17, 57 = 3×19.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(925,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is the value of 5.84 + 14.7 - 3.25?','What is the value of 5.84 + 14.7 - 3.25?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"17.29\", \"18.29\", \"16.89\", \"17.49\"]','17.29','Add 5.84 + 14.7 = 20.54. Subtract 3.25 = 17.29.','Add 5.84 + 14.7 = 20.54. Subtract 3.25 = 17.29.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(926,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Multiply: 3.45 × 100','Multiply: 3.45 × 100','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"34.5\", \"345\", \"3450\", \"0.345\"]','345','Multiplying by 100 moves the decimal point 2 places to the right: 3.45 -> 345.','Multiplying by 100 moves the decimal point 2 places to the right: 3.45 -> 345.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(927,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Divide: 48.6 ÷ 1000','Divide: 48.6 ÷ 1000','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.486\", \"0.0486\", \"4.86\", \"0.00486\"]','0.0486','Dividing by 1000 moves the decimal point 3 places to the left: 0.0486.','Dividing by 1000 moves the decimal point 3 places to the left: 0.0486.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(928,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Write 3,405,020 in words.','Write 3,405,020 in words.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Three million, forty-five thousand and twenty\", \"Three million, four hundred five thousand and twenty\", \"Three million, four hundred fifty thousand and two\", \"Thirty-four million, five thousand and twenty\"]','Three million, four hundred five thousand and twenty','3 millions + 405 thousands + 20 ones.','3 millions + 405 thousands + 20 ones.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(929,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is the common factor of 24 and 36?','What is the common factor of 24 and 36?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8\", \"12\", \"18\", \"9\"]','12','12 divides both 24 (24÷12=2) and 36 (36÷12=3).','12 divides both 24 (24÷12=2) and 36 (36÷12=3).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(930,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Find the Lowest Common Multiple (LCM) of 4, 6, and 8.','Find the Lowest Common Multiple (LCM) of 4, 6, and 8.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"16\", \"24\", \"48\", \"32\"]','24','Multiples of 8: 8, 16, 24. 24 is divisible by 4, 6, and 8.','Multiples of 8: 8, 16, 24. 24 is divisible by 4, 6, and 8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(931,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Find the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of 30 and 45.','Find the Highest Common Factor (HCF) of 30 and 45.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"5\", \"10\", \"15\", \"20\"]','15','Factors of 30: 1,2,3,5,6,10,15,30. Factors of 45: 1,3,5,9,15,45. The highest common is 15.','Factors of 30: 1,2,3,5,6,10,15,30. Factors of 45: 1,3,5,9,15,45. The highest common is 15.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(932,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Solve: 100 - (24 + 36 ÷ 6)','Solve: 100 - (24 + 36 ÷ 6)','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"70\", \"76\", \"64\", \"82\"]','70','Inside bracket: 36÷6 = 6; 24 + 6 = 30. Then 100 - 30 = 70.','Inside bracket: 36÷6 = 6; 24 + 6 = 30. Then 100 - 30 = 70.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(933,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Express 4.075 as a mixed fraction in simplest form.','Express 4.075 as a mixed fraction in simplest form.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"4 3/40\", \"4 7/10\", \"4 1/25\", \"4 3/8\"]','4 3/40','0.075 = 75/1000 = 3/40. So 4 3/40.','0.075 = 75/1000 = 3/40. So 4 3/40.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(934,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is the difference between 80,000 and 34,682?','What is the difference between 80,000 and 34,682?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"45,318\", \"46,318\", \"45,418\", \"46,418\"]','45,318','80,000 - 34,682 = 45,318.','80,000 - 34,682 = 45,318.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(935,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: 250 × 40','Calculate: 250 × 40','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1,000\", \"10,000\", \"100,000\", \"2,500\"]','10,000','25 × 4 = 100. Add two zeros: 10,000.','25 × 4 = 100. Add two zeros: 10,000.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(936,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: 8,400 ÷ 70','Calculate: 8,400 ÷ 70','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"12\", \"120\", \"1,200\", \"140\"]','120','8400 ÷ 70 = 840 ÷ 7 = 120.','8400 ÷ 70 = 840 ÷ 7 = 120.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(937,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is the sum of the first 5 prime numbers?','What is the sum of the first 5 prime numbers?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"28\", \"26\", \"29\", \"18\"]','28','First 5 primes: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11. Sum: 2+3+5+7+11 = 28.','First 5 primes: 2, 3, 5, 7, 11. Sum: 2+3+5+7+11 = 28.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(938,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Round off 3.746 to one decimal place.','Round off 3.746 to one decimal place.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3.7\", \"3.8\", \"3.75\", \"4.0\"]','3.7','The digit in hundredths place is 4 (<5), so round down: 3.7.','The digit in hundredths place is 4 (<5), so round down: 3.7.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(939,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Which number is divisible by 9?','Which number is divisible by 9?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"34,512\", \"45,618\", \"23,415\", \"12,345\"]','45,618','Sum of digits must be a multiple of 9: 4+5+6+1+8 = 24 (no), check 23,415: 2+3+4+1+5=15 (no), check 34,512: 3+4+5+1+2=15 (no), check 45,618 -> 4+5+6+2+1=18 (45,621). Let\'s check 34,515: 3+4+5+1+5 = 18. So 45,621 or 34,515.','Sum of digits must be a multiple of 9: 4+5+6+1+8 = 24 (no), check 23,415: 2+3+4+1+5=15 (no), check 34,512: 3+4+5+1+2=15 (no), check 45,618 -> 4+5+6+2+1=18 (45,621). Let\'s check 34,515: 3+4+5+1+5 = 18. So 45,621 or 34,515.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(940,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Evaluate: 16 + 4 × (10 - 3)','Evaluate: 16 + 4 × (10 - 3)','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"44\", \"140\", \"38\", \"52\"]','44','Bracket: 10 - 3 = 7. Multiply: 4 × 7 = 28. Add: 16 + 28 = 44.','Bracket: 10 - 3 = 7. Multiply: 4 × 7 = 28. Add: 16 + 28 = 44.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(941,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is the digit value of 9 in 8.094?','What is the digit value of 9 in 8.094?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.9\", \"0.09\", \"0.009\", \"9\"]','0.09','9 is in the hundredths place: value is 0.09.','9 is in the hundredths place: value is 0.09.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(942,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: 0.75 × 8','Calculate: 0.75 × 8','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6\", \"0.6\", \"60\", \"5.6\"]','6','3/4 of 8 = 6.','3/4 of 8 = 6.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(943,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Find the missing number: 45,000 + _____ = 100,000','Find the missing number: 45,000 + _____ = 100,000','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"55,000\", \"65,000\", \"50,000\", \"45,000\"]','55,000','100,000 - 45,000 = 55,000.','100,000 - 45,000 = 55,000.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(944,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','How many thousands are there in 5.2 million?','How many thousands are there in 5.2 million?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"520\", \"5,200\", \"52,000\", \"520,000\"]','5,200','5,200,000 ÷ 1,000 = 5,200 thousands.','5,200,000 ÷ 1,000 = 5,200 thousands.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(945,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Calculate: 12.4 ÷ 4','Calculate: 12.4 ÷ 4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3.1\", \"0.31\", \"3.01\", \"3.4\"]','3.1','12 ÷ 4 = 3, 0.4 ÷ 4 = 0.1 -> 3.1.','12 ÷ 4 = 3, 0.4 ÷ 4 = 0.1 -> 3.1.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(946,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','What is 15 squared (15²)?','What is 15 squared (15²)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"225\", \"215\", \"250\", \"175\"]','225','15 × 15 = 225.','15 × 15 = 225.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(947,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Estimate 4,891 × 21 by rounding each to nearest ten.','Estimate 4,891 × 21 by rounding each to nearest ten.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"100,000\", \"98,000\", \"102,000\", \"95,000\"]','98,000','4,890 × 20 = 97,800 ≈ 98,000 (or 5,000 × 20 = 100,000).','4,890 × 20 = 97,800 ≈ 98,000 (or 5,000 × 20 = 100,000).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(948,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Which is greater: 0.65 or 0.605?','Which is greater: 0.65 or 0.605?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.65\", \"0.605\", \"Both are equal\", \"Cannot be determined\"]','0.65','0.650 > 0.605 because 5 hundredths > 0 hundredths.','0.650 > 0.605 because 5 hundredths > 0 hundredths.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(949,'psr_math_numbers','psr_maths','Evaluate: 50 - 5 × 2 + 10','Evaluate: 50 - 5 × 2 + 10','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"50\", \"100\", \"40\", \"80\"]','50','Multiply first: 5 × 2 = 10. Then 50 - 10 = 40. Then 40 + 10 = 50.','Multiply first: 5 × 2 = 10. Then 50 - 10 = 40. Then 40 + 10 = 50.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(950,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Simplify 18/24 to its lowest terms.','Simplify 18/24 to its lowest terms.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3/4\", \"2/3\", \"4/5\", \"6/8\"]','3/4','Divide both numerator and denominator by 6: 18÷6=3, 24÷6=4.','Divide both numerator and denominator by 6: 18÷6=3, 24÷6=4.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(951,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 2/3 + 1/4','Calculate: 2/3 + 1/4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"11/12\", \"3/7\", \"5/12\", \"7/12\"]','11/12','Common denominator 12: 8/12 + 3/12 = 11/12.','Common denominator 12: 8/12 + 3/12 = 11/12.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(952,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 3 1/2 - 1 3/4','Calculate: 3 1/2 - 1 3/4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1 3/4\", \"1 1/2\", \"2 1/4\", \"1 1/4\"]','1 3/4','3 2/4 - 1 3/4 = 2 6/4 - 1 3/4 = 1 3/4.','3 2/4 - 1 3/4 = 2 6/4 - 1 3/4 = 1 3/4.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(953,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Multiply: 2/5 × 15/16','Multiply: 2/5 × 15/16','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3/8\", \"3/10\", \"1/4\", \"5/8\"]','3/8','(2×15)/(5×16) = 30/80 = 3/8.','(2×15)/(5×16) = 30/80 = 3/8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(954,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Divide: 3/4 ÷ 6','Divide: 3/4 ÷ 6','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/8\", \"1/4\", \"9/2\", \"1/2\"]','1/8','3/4 × 1/6 = 3/24 = 1/8.','3/4 × 1/6 = 3/24 = 1/8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(955,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Convert 7/8 into a decimal.','Convert 7/8 into a decimal.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.875\", \"0.78\", \"0.85\", \"0.75\"]','0.875','7 ÷ 8 = 0.875.','7 ÷ 8 = 0.875.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(956,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','What is 2/3 of 450 BND?','What is 2/3 of 450 BND?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"300 BND\", \"150 BND\", \"350 BND\", \"250 BND\"]','300 BND','450 ÷ 3 = 150. 150 × 2 = 300 BND.','450 ÷ 3 = 150. 150 × 2 = 300 BND.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(957,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Convert 2 3/5 into an improper fraction.','Convert 2 3/5 into an improper fraction.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"13/5\", \"11/5\", \"15/5\", \"10/5\"]','13/5','(2 × 5 + 3) / 5 = 13/5.','(2 × 5 + 3) / 5 = 13/5.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(958,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Convert 17/4 into a mixed number.','Convert 17/4 into a mixed number.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"4 1/4\", \"3 3/4\", \"4 3/4\", \"5 1/4\"]','4 1/4','17 ÷ 4 = 4 with remainder 1 -> 4 1/4.','17 ÷ 4 = 4 with remainder 1 -> 4 1/4.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(959,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Arrange in ascending order: 1/2, 2/5, 3/4','Arrange in ascending order: 1/2, 2/5, 3/4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"2/5, 1/2, 3/4\", \"1/2, 2/5, 3/4\", \"3/4, 1/2, 2/5\", \"2/5, 3/4, 1/2\"]','2/5, 1/2, 3/4','In decimals: 2/5 = 0.4, 1/2 = 0.5, 3/4 = 0.75. So 2/5 < 1/2 < 3/4.','In decimals: 2/5 = 0.4, 1/2 = 0.5, 3/4 = 0.75. So 2/5 < 1/2 < 3/4.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(960,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 4 - 2 3/8','Calculate: 4 - 2 3/8','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1 5/8\", \"2 5/8\", \"1 3/8\", \"2 3/8\"]','1 5/8','3 8/8 - 2 3/8 = 1 5/8.','3 8/8 - 2 3/8 = 1 5/8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(961,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 1 1/3 × 2 1/4','Calculate: 1 1/3 × 2 1/4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3\", \"2 1/12\", \"3 1/4\", \"2 2/3\"]','3','4/3 × 9/4 = 36/12 = 3.','4/3 × 9/4 = 36/12 = 3.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(962,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','What is the reciprocal of 5/7?','What is the reciprocal of 5/7?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"7/5\", \"5/7\", \"1 1/5\", \"2/7\"]','7/5','Invert the fraction: numerator and denominator swap.','Invert the fraction: numerator and denominator swap.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(963,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','A ribbon of length 6 meters is cut into pieces of 3/4 meter each. How many pieces are there?','A ribbon of length 6 meters is cut into pieces of 3/4 meter each. How many pieces are there?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8\", \"6\", \"9\", \"7\"]','8','6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = 8 pieces.','6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = 8 pieces.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(964,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Add: 0.45 + 3/10','Add: 0.45 + 3/10','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.75\", \"0.48\", \"0.85\", \"0.70\"]','0.75','3/10 = 0.30. 0.45 + 0.30 = 0.75.','3/10 = 0.30. 0.45 + 0.30 = 0.75.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(965,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Subtract: 5/6 - 2/3','Subtract: 5/6 - 2/3','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/6\", \"1/3\", \"3/6\", \"1/12\"]','1/6','5/6 - 4/6 = 1/6.','5/6 - 4/6 = 1/6.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(966,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Find the value of 5 ÷ 1/2','Find the value of 5 ÷ 1/2','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"10\", \"2.5\", \"5.5\", \"15\"]','10','5 × 2/1 = 10.','5 × 2/1 = 10.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(967,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Which fraction is equivalent to 0.6?','Which fraction is equivalent to 0.6?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3/5\", \"2/3\", \"6/100\", \"5/8\"]','3/5','6/10 = 3/5.','6/10 = 3/5.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(968,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Amin has 120 marbles. He gives 3/8 of them to his friend. How many marbles does he have left?','Amin has 120 marbles. He gives 3/8 of them to his friend. How many marbles does he have left?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"75\", \"45\", \"80\", \"65\"]','75','Given away: 3/8 × 120 = 45. Remaining: 120 - 45 = 75.','Given away: 3/8 × 120 = 45. Remaining: 120 - 45 = 75.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(969,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','What fraction of 1 hour is 24 minutes?','What fraction of 1 hour is 24 minutes?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"2/5\", \"1/3\", \"3/5\", \"4/15\"]','2/5','24/60 = divide by 12 = 2/5.','24/60 = divide by 12 = 2/5.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(970,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Solve: 2/7 of a number is 14. What is the number?','Solve: 2/7 of a number is 14. What is the number?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"49\", \"28\", \"35\", \"56\"]','49','1/7 is 14 ÷ 2 = 7. Whole number is 7 × 7 = 49.','1/7 is 14 ÷ 2 = 7. Whole number is 7 × 7 = 49.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(971,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 1/2 + 1/3 + 1/6','Calculate: 1/2 + 1/3 + 1/6','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1\", \"5/6\", \"1 1/6\", \"2/3\"]','1','3/6 + 2/6 + 1/6 = 6/6 = 1.','3/6 + 2/6 + 1/6 = 6/6 = 1.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(972,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Express 0.125 as a fraction in lowest terms.','Express 0.125 as a fraction in lowest terms.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/8\", \"1/4\", \"1/5\", \"3/8\"]','1/8','125/1000 = 1/8.','125/1000 = 1/8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(973,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Divide: 2 1/2 ÷ 5','Divide: 2 1/2 ÷ 5','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/2\", \"1\", \"2\", \"1/4\"]','1/2','5/2 × 1/5 = 5/10 = 1/2.','5/2 × 1/5 = 5/10 = 1/2.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(974,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Which fraction is larger: 5/9 or 7/12?','Which fraction is larger: 5/9 or 7/12?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"7/12\", \"5/9\", \"Both are equal\", \"Cannot be determined\"]','7/12','5/9 ≈ 0.555; 7/12 ≈ 0.583. 7/12 is greater.','5/9 ≈ 0.555; 7/12 ≈ 0.583. 7/12 is greater.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(975,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Multiply: 0.6 × 0.4','Multiply: 0.6 × 0.4','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.24\", \"2.4\", \"0.024\", \"0.4\"]','0.24','6 × 4 = 24. Two decimal places: 0.24.','6 × 4 = 24. Two decimal places: 0.24.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(976,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Convert 15/20 to a percentage.','Convert 15/20 to a percentage.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"75%\", \"80%\", \"70%\", \"65%\"]','75%','15/20 = 3/4 = 75%.','15/20 = 3/4 = 75%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(977,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','Calculate: 10 - 3.42','Calculate: 10 - 3.42','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6.58\", \"6.68\", \"7.58\", \"6.48\"]','6.58','10.00 - 3.42 = 6.58.','10.00 - 3.42 = 6.58.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(978,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','If 3/4 kg of grapes costs $6, how much does 1 kg cost?','If 3/4 kg of grapes costs $6, how much does 1 kg cost?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$8\", \"$9\", \"$7.50\", \"$8.50\"]','$8','6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = $8.','6 ÷ 3/4 = 6 × 4/3 = $8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(979,'psr_math_fractions_decimals','psr_maths','What is 1.5 + 2 1/4 in decimal form?','What is 1.5 + 2 1/4 in decimal form?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3.75\", \"3.5\", \"3.25\", \"4.0\"]','3.75','2 1/4 = 2.25. 1.5 + 2.25 = 3.75.','2 1/4 = 2.25. 1.5 + 2.25 = 3.75.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(980,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Express 35% as a fraction in simplest form.','Express 35% as a fraction in simplest form.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"7/20\", \"3/10\", \"7/10\", \"1/4\"]','7/20','35/100 = 7/20 by dividing numerator and denominator by 5.','35/100 = 7/20 by dividing numerator and denominator by 5.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(981,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','What is 20% of 350 BND?','What is 20% of 350 BND?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"70 BND\", \"60 BND\", \"80 BND\", \"50 BND\"]','70 BND','20/100 × 350 = 1/5 × 350 = 70 BND.','20/100 × 350 = 1/5 × 350 = 70 BND.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(982,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A school bag costs $50. A 15% discount is given. What is the sale price?','A school bag costs $50. A 15% discount is given. What is the sale price?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$42.50\", \"$40.00\", \"$45.00\", \"$37.50\"]','$42.50','Discount = 15% of $50 = $7.50. Sale price = $50 - $7.50 = $42.50.','Discount = 15% of $50 = $7.50. Sale price = $50 - $7.50 = $42.50.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(983,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','In a class of 40 students, 24 are girls. What percentage of the class are boys?','In a class of 40 students, 24 are girls. What percentage of the class are boys?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"40%\", \"60%\", \"30%\", \"45%\"]','40%','Boys = 40 - 24 = 16. Percentage = (16/40) × 100% = 40%.','Boys = 40 - 24 = 16. Percentage = (16/40) × 100% = 40%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(984,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','The ratio of red balls to blue balls is 3 : 5. If there are 15 red balls, how many blue balls are there?','The ratio of red balls to blue balls is 3 : 5. If there are 15 red balls, how many blue balls are there?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"25\", \"20\", \"30\", \"35\"]','25','3 units = 15 -> 1 unit = 5. Blue balls = 5 × 5 = 25.','3 units = 15 -> 1 unit = 5. Blue balls = 5 × 5 = 25.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(985,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Express 4:5 as a percentage.','Express 4:5 as a percentage.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"80%\", \"75%\", \"85%\", \"60%\"]','80%','4/5 × 100% = 80%.','4/5 × 100% = 80%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(986,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','An article was bought for $80 and sold for $100. What is the percentage profit?','An article was bought for $80 and sold for $100. What is the percentage profit?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"25%\", \"20%\", \"15%\", \"30%\"]','25%','Profit = $100 - $80 = $20. % Profit = (20/80) × 100% = 25%.','Profit = $100 - $80 = $20. % Profit = (20/80) × 100% = 25%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(987,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Divide $180 between Ali and Abu in the ratio 4 : 5. How much does Abu get?','Divide $180 between Ali and Abu in the ratio 4 : 5. How much does Abu get?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$100\", \"$80\", \"$90\", \"$110\"]','$100','Total units = 4 + 5 = 9. 1 unit = $180 ÷ 9 = $20. Abu gets 5 × $20 = $100.','Total units = 4 + 5 = 9. 1 unit = $180 ÷ 9 = $20. Abu gets 5 × $20 = $100.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(988,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Convert 0.08 into a percentage.','Convert 0.08 into a percentage.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8%\", \"80%\", \"0.8%\", \"0.08%\"]','8%','Multiply 0.08 by 100 = 8%.','Multiply 0.08 by 100 = 8%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(989,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','There are 500 books in a library. 45% are fiction. How many non-fiction books are there?','There are 500 books in a library. 45% are fiction. How many non-fiction books are there?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"275\", \"225\", \"250\", \"300\"]','275','Non-fiction = 100% - 45% = 55%. 55% of 500 = 55 × 5 = 275.','Non-fiction = 100% - 45% = 55%. 55% of 500 = 55 × 5 = 275.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(990,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','What is the ratio of 45 minutes to 2 hours in simplest form?','What is the ratio of 45 minutes to 2 hours in simplest form?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3 : 8\", \"3 : 4\", \"9 : 20\", \"1 : 3\"]','3 : 8','2 hours = 120 minutes. 45 : 120 = divide by 15 = 3 : 8.','2 hours = 120 minutes. 45 : 120 = divide by 15 = 3 : 8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(991,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Increase $240 by 25%.','Increase $240 by 25%.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$300\", \"$280\", \"$320\", \"$260\"]','$300','25% of 240 = 60. $240 + $60 = $300.','25% of 240 = 60. $240 + $60 = $300.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(992,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Decrease 80 kg by 10%.','Decrease 80 kg by 10%.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"72 kg\", \"70 kg\", \"74 kg\", \"68 kg\"]','72 kg','10% of 80 = 8. 80 - 8 = 72 kg.','10% of 80 = 8. 80 - 8 = 72 kg.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(993,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A television original price is $600. It is sold for $480. What is the percentage discount?','A television original price is $600. It is sold for $480. What is the percentage discount?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"20%\", \"25%\", \"15%\", \"18%\"]','20%','Discount = $600 - $480 = $120. % Discount = (120/600) × 100% = 20%.','Discount = $600 - $480 = $120. % Discount = (120/600) × 100% = 20%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(994,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','If 5 kg of rice costs $12.50, how much will 8 kg cost?','If 5 kg of rice costs $12.50, how much will 8 kg cost?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$20.00\", \"$18.50\", \"$22.00\", \"$19.00\"]','$20.00','Cost of 1 kg = $12.50 ÷ 5 = $2.50. Cost of 8 kg = 8 × $2.50 = $20.00.','Cost of 1 kg = $12.50 ÷ 5 = $2.50. Cost of 8 kg = 8 × $2.50 = $20.00.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(995,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','The ratio of boys to girls in a hall is 5 : 7. If there are 84 girls, what is the total number of students?','The ratio of boys to girls in a hall is 5 : 7. If there are 84 girls, what is the total number of students?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"144\", \"120\", \"136\", \"150\"]','144','7 units = 84 -> 1 unit = 12. Total units = 5+7=12. Total = 12 × 12 = 144.','7 units = 84 -> 1 unit = 12. Total units = 5+7=12. Total = 12 × 12 = 144.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(996,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Express 125% as a decimal.','Express 125% as a decimal.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1.25\", \"12.5\", \"0.125\", \"125.0\"]','1.25','125 ÷ 100 = 1.25.','125 ÷ 100 = 1.25.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(997,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Find 150% of 80.','Find 150% of 80.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"120\", \"100\", \"140\", \"160\"]','120','1.5 × 80 = 120.','1.5 × 80 = 120.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(998,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A trader bought a watch for $150 and sold it at a loss of 10%. What was the selling price?','A trader bought a watch for $150 and sold it at a loss of 10%. What was the selling price?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$135\", \"$140\", \"$130\", \"$125\"]','$135','Loss = 10% of 150 = $15. Selling price = 150 - 15 = $135.','Loss = 10% of 150 = $15. Selling price = 150 - 15 = $135.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(999,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','What percentage of 2 kg is 500 g?','What percentage of 2 kg is 500 g?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"25%\", \"20%\", \"30%\", \"15%\"]','25%','2 kg = 2000 g. (500/2000) × 100% = 25%.','2 kg = 2000 g. (500/2000) × 100% = 25%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1000,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','In a survey, 60% of 800 respondents chose chocolate. How many did not choose chocolate?','In a survey, 60% of 800 respondents chose chocolate. How many did not choose chocolate?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"320\", \"480\", \"300\", \"350\"]','320','Did not choose = 40%. 40% of 800 = 0.4 × 800 = 320.','Did not choose = 40%. 40% of 800 = 0.4 × 800 = 320.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1001,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Simplify the ratio 2.4 : 3.6.','Simplify the ratio 2.4 : 3.6.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"2 : 3\", \"3 : 4\", \"4 : 5\", \"1 : 2\"]','2 : 3','Multiply by 10 -> 24 : 36. Divide by 12 -> 2 : 3.','Multiply by 10 -> 24 : 36. Divide by 12 -> 2 : 3.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1002,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A car travels 180 km in 3 hours. What is its speed?','A car travels 180 km in 3 hours. What is its speed?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"60 km/h\", \"50 km/h\", \"70 km/h\", \"55 km/h\"]','60 km/h','Speed = Distance ÷ Time = 180 ÷ 3 = 60 km/h.','Speed = Distance ÷ Time = 180 ÷ 3 = 60 km/h.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1003,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','What is 7.5% written as a decimal?','What is 7.5% written as a decimal?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0.075\", \"0.75\", \"0.0075\", \"7.5\"]','0.075','7.5 ÷ 100 = 0.075.','7.5 ÷ 100 = 0.075.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1004,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Three numbers are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. If their sum is 100, what is the largest number?','Three numbers are in the ratio 2 : 3 : 5. If their sum is 100, what is the largest number?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"50\", \"40\", \"30\", \"60\"]','50','Total parts = 2+3+5=10. 1 part = 100÷10 = 10. Largest = 5 × 10 = 50.','Total parts = 2+3+5=10. 1 part = 100÷10 = 10. Largest = 5 × 10 = 50.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1005,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A phone battery was at 90%. After usage, it dropped to 45%. What percentage was consumed?','A phone battery was at 90%. After usage, it dropped to 45%. What percentage was consumed?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"45%\", \"50%\", \"40%\", \"35%\"]','45%','90% - 45% = 45%.','90% - 45% = 45%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1006,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Calculate the simple interest on $1,000 at 5% per annum for 2 years.','Calculate the simple interest on $1,000 at 5% per annum for 2 years.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$100\", \"$50\", \"$200\", \"$150\"]','$100','I = (P × R × T)/100 = (1000 × 5 × 2)/100 = $100.','I = (P × R × T)/100 = (1000 × 5 × 2)/100 = $100.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1007,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A recipe uses 3 cups of flour for every 2 cups of sugar. If 9 cups of flour are used, how much sugar is needed?','A recipe uses 3 cups of flour for every 2 cups of sugar. If 9 cups of flour are used, how much sugar is needed?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6 cups\", \"5 cups\", \"8 cups\", \"4 cups\"]','6 cups','Ratio 3:2. 9 is 3×3, so sugar = 2 × 3 = 6 cups.','Ratio 3:2. 9 is 3×3, so sugar = 2 × 3 = 6 cups.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1008,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','Which is greater: 1/4 or 22%?','Which is greater: 1/4 or 22%?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/4\", \"22%\", \"Both are equal\", \"Cannot be determined\"]','1/4','1/4 = 25%. 25% > 22%.','1/4 = 25%. 25% > 22%.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1009,'psr_math_percentages_ratios','psr_maths','A jacket priced at $120 is sold at a 30% discount. How much money was saved?','A jacket priced at $120 is sold at a 30% discount. How much money was saved?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"$36\", \"$84\", \"$40\", \"$30\"]','$36','Discount saved = 30% of $120 = 0.30 × 120 = $36.','Discount saved = 30% of $120 = 0.30 × 120 = $36.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1010,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Convert 4.5 kilometers into meters.','Convert 4.5 kilometers into meters.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"4,500 m\", \"450 m\", \"45,000 m\", \"45 m\"]','4,500 m','1 km = 1,000 m. 4.5 × 1,000 = 4,500 m.','1 km = 1,000 m. 4.5 × 1,000 = 4,500 m.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1011,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Find the perimeter of a rectangle with length 14 cm and width 8 cm.','Find the perimeter of a rectangle with length 14 cm and width 8 cm.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"44 cm\", \"112 cm\", \"22 cm\", \"48 cm\"]','44 cm','Perimeter = 2 × (length + width) = 2 × (14 + 8) = 2 × 22 = 44 cm.','Perimeter = 2 × (length + width) = 2 × (14 + 8) = 2 × 22 = 44 cm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1012,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Calculate the area of a right-angled triangle with base 10 cm and height 7 cm.','Calculate the area of a right-angled triangle with base 10 cm and height 7 cm.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"35 cm²\", \"70 cm²\", \"17 cm²\", \"40 cm²\"]','35 cm²','Area = 1/2 × base × height = 1/2 × 10 × 7 = 35 cm².','Area = 1/2 × base × height = 1/2 × 10 × 7 = 35 cm².','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1013,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A cube has sides of length 5 cm. What is its volume?','A cube has sides of length 5 cm. What is its volume?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"125 cm³\", \"25 cm³\", \"150 cm³\", \"100 cm³\"]','125 cm³','Volume of cube = s³ = 5 × 5 × 5 = 125 cm³.','Volume of cube = s³ = 5 × 5 × 5 = 125 cm³.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1014,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Convert 3,250 milliliters into liters.','Convert 3,250 milliliters into liters.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3.25 L\", \"32.5 L\", \"0.325 L\", \"325 L\"]','3.25 L','1 L = 1,000 ml. 3,250 ÷ 1,000 = 3.25 L.','1 L = 1,000 ml. 3,250 ÷ 1,000 = 3.25 L.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1015,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','What is the sum of angles on a straight line?','What is the sum of angles on a straight line?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"180°\", \"360°\", \"90°\", \"270°\"]','180°','Angles on a straight line always add up to 180°.','Angles on a straight line always add up to 180°.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1016,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','In a triangle, two angles measure 65° and 45°. What is the third angle?','In a triangle, two angles measure 65° and 45°. What is the third angle?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"70°\", \"80°\", \"60°\", \"75°\"]','70°','Sum of angles in a triangle = 180°. 180 - (65 + 45) = 180 - 110 = 70°.','Sum of angles in a triangle = 180°. 180 - (65 + 45) = 180 - 110 = 70°.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1017,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A rectangular tank is 20 cm long, 10 cm wide, and 15 cm high. What is its capacity in liters?','A rectangular tank is 20 cm long, 10 cm wide, and 15 cm high. What is its capacity in liters?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3 L\", \"30 L\", \"300 L\", \"0.3 L\"]','3 L','Volume = 20 × 10 × 15 = 3,000 cm³. 1,000 cm³ = 1 L, so 3,000 cm³ = 3 L.','Volume = 20 × 10 × 15 = 3,000 cm³. 1,000 cm³ = 1 L, so 3,000 cm³ = 3 L.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1018,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A movie starts at 14:45 and lasts for 2 hours and 15 minutes. What time does it end?','A movie starts at 14:45 and lasts for 2 hours and 15 minutes. What time does it end?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"17:00\", \"16:45\", \"17:15\", \"16:50\"]','17:00','14:45 + 2h = 16:45. 16:45 + 15 min = 17:00.','14:45 + 2h = 16:45. 16:45 + 15 min = 17:00.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1019,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Find the perimeter of a regular hexagon with sides of length 7 cm.','Find the perimeter of a regular hexagon with sides of length 7 cm.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"42 cm\", \"35 cm\", \"49 cm\", \"28 cm\"]','42 cm','A regular hexagon has 6 equal sides: 6 × 7 = 42 cm.','A regular hexagon has 6 equal sides: 6 × 7 = 42 cm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1020,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Convert 2.75 kg into grams.','Convert 2.75 kg into grams.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"2,750 g\", \"275 g\", \"27,500 g\", \"27.5 g\"]','2,750 g','1 kg = 1,000 g. 2.75 × 1,000 = 2,750 g.','1 kg = 1,000 g. 2.75 × 1,000 = 2,750 g.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1021,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','The area of a square is 64 cm². What is the length of each side?','The area of a square is 64 cm². What is the length of each side?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8 cm\", \"16 cm\", \"32 cm\", \"4 cm\"]','8 cm','Area = side × side. √64 = 8 cm.','Area = side × side. √64 = 8 cm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1022,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','What is an angle measuring 135° called?','What is an angle measuring 135° called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Obtuse angle\", \"Acute angle\", \"Right angle\", \"Reflex angle\"]','Obtuse angle','Angles between 90° and 180° are obtuse.','Angles between 90° and 180° are obtuse.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1023,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','How many vertices does a cuboid have?','How many vertices does a cuboid have?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8\", \"6\", \"12\", \"10\"]','8','A cuboid has 6 faces, 12 edges, and 8 vertices (corners).','A cuboid has 6 faces, 12 edges, and 8 vertices (corners).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1024,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A square garden has a perimeter of 48 m. What is its area?','A square garden has a perimeter of 48 m. What is its area?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"144 m²\", \"96 m²\", \"196 m²\", \"120 m²\"]','144 m²','Side length = 48 ÷ 4 = 12 m. Area = 12 × 12 = 144 m².','Side length = 48 ÷ 4 = 12 m. Area = 12 × 12 = 144 m².','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1025,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Convert 4 hours and 25 minutes into minutes.','Convert 4 hours and 25 minutes into minutes.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"265 minutes\", \"240 minutes\", \"250 minutes\", \"285 minutes\"]','265 minutes','4 × 60 = 240. 240 + 25 = 265 minutes.','4 × 60 = 240. 240 + 25 = 265 minutes.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1026,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Two complementary angles add up to how many degrees?','Two complementary angles add up to how many degrees?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"90°\", \"180°\", \"360°\", \"45°\"]','90°','Complementary angles sum to 90°. Supplementary angles sum to 180°.','Complementary angles sum to 90°. Supplementary angles sum to 180°.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1027,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A bus traveled 240 km at an average speed of 80 km/h. How long did the trip take?','A bus traveled 240 km at an average speed of 80 km/h. How long did the trip take?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3 hours\", \"4 hours\", \"2.5 hours\", \"3.5 hours\"]','3 hours','Time = Distance ÷ Speed = 240 ÷ 80 = 3 hours.','Time = Distance ÷ Speed = 240 ÷ 80 = 3 hours.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1028,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Calculate the volume of a cuboid with length 8 cm, width 6 cm, and height 5 cm.','Calculate the volume of a cuboid with length 8 cm, width 6 cm, and height 5 cm.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"240 cm³\", \"190 cm³\", \"120 cm³\", \"280 cm³\"]','240 cm³','Volume = l × w × h = 8 × 6 × 5 = 240 cm³.','Volume = l × w × h = 8 × 6 × 5 = 240 cm³.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1029,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','What is the surface area of a cube with side 3 cm?','What is the surface area of a cube with side 3 cm?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"54 cm²\", \"27 cm²\", \"36 cm²\", \"18 cm²\"]','54 cm²','Surface area = 6 × s² = 6 × (3×3) = 6 × 9 = 54 cm².','Surface area = 6 × s² = 6 × (3×3) = 6 × 9 = 54 cm².','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1030,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','How many lines of symmetry does an equilateral triangle have?','How many lines of symmetry does an equilateral triangle have?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3\", \"1\", \"2\", \"6\"]','3','An equilateral triangle has 3 equal sides and 3 lines of symmetry.','An equilateral triangle has 3 equal sides and 3 lines of symmetry.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1031,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A fence of 60 m encloses a rectangular field of width 12 m. What is the length of the field?','A fence of 60 m encloses a rectangular field of width 12 m. What is the length of the field?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"18 m\", \"24 m\", \"20 m\", \"15 m\"]','18 m','Half perimeter = 60 ÷ 2 = 30 m. Length = 30 - 12 = 18 m.','Half perimeter = 60 ÷ 2 = 30 m. Length = 30 - 12 = 18 m.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1032,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Convert 500 cm into meters.','Convert 500 cm into meters.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"5 m\", \"50 m\", \"0.5 m\", \"500 m\"]','5 m','1 m = 100 cm. 500 ÷ 100 = 5 m.','1 m = 100 cm. 500 ÷ 100 = 5 m.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1033,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','An angle at a point completes a full circle. What is its measure?','An angle at a point completes a full circle. What is its measure?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"360°\", \"180°\", \"270°\", \"90°\"]','360°','Angles around a full point sum to 360°.','Angles around a full point sum to 360°.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1034,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A water bottle has 750 ml of water. If Sarah drinks 0.4 L, how much is left?','A water bottle has 750 ml of water. If Sarah drinks 0.4 L, how much is left?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"350 ml\", \"300 ml\", \"400 ml\", \"250 ml\"]','350 ml','0.4 L = 400 ml. 750 - 400 = 350 ml.','0.4 L = 400 ml. 750 - 400 = 350 ml.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1035,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Find the perimeter of an isosceles triangle with sides 10 cm, 10 cm, and 6 cm.','Find the perimeter of an isosceles triangle with sides 10 cm, 10 cm, and 6 cm.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"26 cm\", \"20 cm\", \"24 cm\", \"28 cm\"]','26 cm','Perimeter = 10 + 10 + 6 = 26 cm.','Perimeter = 10 + 10 + 6 = 26 cm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1036,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','What is the area of a parallelogram with base 12 cm and height 5 cm?','What is the area of a parallelogram with base 12 cm and height 5 cm?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"60 cm²\", \"30 cm²\", \"45 cm²\", \"72 cm²\"]','60 cm²','Area of parallelogram = base × height = 12 × 5 = 60 cm².','Area of parallelogram = base × height = 12 × 5 = 60 cm².','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1037,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','Express 15:30 in 12-hour clock format.','Express 15:30 in 12-hour clock format.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3:30 p.m.\", \"3:30 a.m.\", \"5:30 p.m.\", \"1:30 p.m.\"]','3:30 p.m.','15:30 - 12:00 = 3:30 p.m.','15:30 - 12:00 = 3:30 p.m.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1038,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','A bag of flour weighs 2 kg 400 g. 650 g is used for baking. What is the remaining mass?','A bag of flour weighs 2 kg 400 g. 650 g is used for baking. What is the remaining mass?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1 kg 750 g\", \"1 kg 850 g\", \"1 kg 650 g\", \"1 kg 950 g\"]','1 kg 750 g','2,400 g - 650 g = 1,750 g = 1 kg 750 g.','2,400 g - 650 g = 1,750 g = 1 kg 750 g.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1039,'psr_math_measurement_geometry','psr_maths','How many edges does a triangular prism have?','How many edges does a triangular prism have?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"9\", \"6\", \"8\", \"12\"]','9','A triangular prism has 5 faces, 6 vertices, and 9 edges.','A triangular prism has 5 faces, 6 vertices, and 9 edges.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1040,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','Find the mean (average) of these numbers: 12, 16, 20, 24, 28.','Find the mean (average) of these numbers: 12, 16, 20, 24, 28.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"20\", \"18\", \"22\", \"24\"]','20','Sum = 12+16+20+24+28 = 100. Mean = 100 ÷ 5 = 20.','Sum = 12+16+20+24+28 = 100. Mean = 100 ÷ 5 = 20.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1041,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','The total score of 4 tests is 320. What is the average score per test?','The total score of 4 tests is 320. What is the average score per test?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"80\", \"75\", \"85\", \"70\"]','80','Average = Total score ÷ number of tests = 320 ÷ 4 = 80.','Average = Total score ÷ number of tests = 320 ÷ 4 = 80.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1042,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a bar chart, each grid square represents 5 students. A bar is 6 squares tall. How many students does it represent?','In a bar chart, each grid square represents 5 students. A bar is 6 squares tall. How many students does it represent?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"30\", \"25\", \"35\", \"20\"]','30','6 squares × 5 students per square = 30 students.','6 squares × 5 students per square = 30 students.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1043,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','What is the median of the following set: 3, 7, 8, 12, 15?','What is the median of the following set: 3, 7, 8, 12, 15?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"8\", \"7\", \"10\", \"12\"]','8','The numbers are in order; the middle number is 8.','The numbers are in order; the middle number is 8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1044,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a pictogram, 1 symbol represents 8 books. How many symbols are needed for 48 books?','In a pictogram, 1 symbol represents 8 books. How many symbols are needed for 48 books?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6\", \"5\", \"7\", \"8\"]','6','48 ÷ 8 = 6 symbols.','48 ÷ 8 = 6 symbols.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1045,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','The average mass of 3 boys is 42 kg. What is their total mass?','The average mass of 3 boys is 42 kg. What is their total mass?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"126 kg\", \"120 kg\", \"132 kg\", \"124 kg\"]','126 kg','Total mass = Average × count = 42 × 3 = 126 kg.','Total mass = Average × count = 42 × 3 = 126 kg.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1046,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A pie chart represents 120 students. A sector of 90° represents students who play football. How many students play football?','A pie chart represents 120 students. A sector of 90° represents students who play football. How many students play football?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"30\", \"40\", \"25\", \"35\"]','30','90°/360° = 1/4. 1/4 of 120 = 30 students.','90°/360° = 1/4. 1/4 of 120 = 30 students.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1047,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','Find the range of the numbers: 15, 23, 8, 42, 19.','Find the range of the numbers: 15, 23, 8, 42, 19.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"34\", \"30\", \"32\", \"28\"]','34','Range = Maximum - Minimum = 42 - 8 = 34.','Range = Maximum - Minimum = 42 - 8 = 34.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1048,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','What is the mode of: 4, 6, 8, 6, 9, 6, 10, 8?','What is the mode of: 4, 6, 8, 6, 9, 6, 10, 8?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6\", \"8\", \"7\", \"9\"]','6','6 appears most frequently (3 times).','6 appears most frequently (3 times).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1049,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','Four children have an average height of 135 cm. If a fifth child of height 145 cm joins, what is the new average?','Four children have an average height of 135 cm. If a fifth child of height 145 cm joins, what is the new average?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"137 cm\", \"136 cm\", \"138 cm\", \"140 cm\"]','137 cm','Initial total = 4 × 135 = 540. New total = 540 + 145 = 685. New average = 685 ÷ 5 = 137 cm.','Initial total = 4 × 135 = 540. New total = 540 + 145 = 685. New average = 685 ÷ 5 = 137 cm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1050,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A dice is rolled once. What is the probability of getting an even number?','A dice is rolled once. What is the probability of getting an even number?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/2\", \"1/3\", \"1/6\", \"2/3\"]','1/2','Even numbers on a dice: 2, 4, 6 (3 out of 6) = 3/6 = 1/2.','Even numbers on a dice: 2, 4, 6 (3 out of 6) = 3/6 = 1/2.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1051,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A bag contains 3 red, 4 blue, and 5 green marbles. What is the probability of picking a blue marble?','A bag contains 3 red, 4 blue, and 5 green marbles. What is the probability of picking a blue marble?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/3\", \"1/4\", \"5/12\", \"1/2\"]','1/3','Total marbles = 3+4+5=12. Blue = 4/12 = 1/3.','Total marbles = 3+4+5=12. Blue = 4/12 = 1/3.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1052,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','The average temperature of 5 days was 31°C. What was the sum of temperatures over the 5 days?','The average temperature of 5 days was 31°C. What was the sum of temperatures over the 5 days?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"155°C\", \"150°C\", \"160°C\", \"165°C\"]','155°C','Total = 5 × 31 = 155°C.','Total = 5 × 31 = 155°C.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1053,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','If the mean of 6, 8, x, and 12 is 9, what is the value of x?','If the mean of 6, 8, x, and 12 is 9, what is the value of x?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"10\", \"8\", \"11\", \"9\"]','10','Sum must be 4 × 9 = 36. 6 + 8 + 12 = 26. x = 36 - 26 = 10.','Sum must be 4 × 9 = 36. 6 + 8 + 12 = 26. x = 36 - 26 = 10.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1054,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a pie chart, a sector measuring 180° represents what fraction of the whole data?','In a pie chart, a sector measuring 180° represents what fraction of the whole data?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/2\", \"1/4\", \"3/4\", \"1/3\"]','1/2','180° / 360° = 1/2.','180° / 360° = 1/2.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1055,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A card is drawn from a standard deck of 52 playing cards. What is the probability of drawing an Ace?','A card is drawn from a standard deck of 52 playing cards. What is the probability of drawing an Ace?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/13\", \"1/4\", \"1/52\", \"4/13\"]','1/13','There are 4 Aces in 52 cards: 4/52 = 1/13.','There are 4 Aces in 52 cards: 4/52 = 1/13.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1056,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','Find the mean of 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, and 5.5.','Find the mean of 2.5, 3.5, 4.5, and 5.5.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"4.0\", \"3.8\", \"4.2\", \"4.5\"]','4.0','Sum = 16.0. Mean = 16.0 ÷ 4 = 4.0.','Sum = 16.0. Mean = 16.0 ÷ 4 = 4.0.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1057,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a bar chart, the height of bar for Year 6 is 45 and Year 5 is 30. How many more Year 6 students are there?','In a bar chart, the height of bar for Year 6 is 45 and Year 5 is 30. How many more Year 6 students are there?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"15\", \"10\", \"20\", \"25\"]','15','45 - 30 = 15 students.','45 - 30 = 15 students.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1058,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','What is the probability of an impossible event?','What is the probability of an impossible event?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0\", \"1\", \"0.5\", \"-1\"]','0','Probability ranges from 0 (impossible) to 1 (certain).','Probability ranges from 0 (impossible) to 1 (certain).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1059,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','What is the median of: 14, 18, 20, 22, 26, 30?','What is the median of: 14, 18, 20, 22, 26, 30?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"21\", \"20\", \"22\", \"20.5\"]','21','Even count (6 items): average the middle two (20 + 22) ÷ 2 = 21.','Even count (6 items): average the middle two (20 + 22) ÷ 2 = 21.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1060,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A coin is flipped twice. What is the probability of getting two heads (HH)?','A coin is flipped twice. What is the probability of getting two heads (HH)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"1/4\", \"1/2\", \"3/4\", \"1/8\"]','1/4','Outcomes: HH, HT, TH, TT (4 outcomes). Probability of HH = 1/4.','Outcomes: HH, HT, TH, TT (4 outcomes). Probability of HH = 1/4.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1061,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A student scores 70, 80, 85, and 95 in four tests. What is his mean score?','A student scores 70, 80, 85, and 95 in four tests. What is his mean score?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"82.5\", \"80.0\", \"85.0\", \"83.5\"]','82.5','Sum = 330. Mean = 330 ÷ 4 = 82.5.','Sum = 330. Mean = 330 ÷ 4 = 82.5.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1062,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a pictogram, a car icon represents 20 vehicles. What does half an icon represent?','In a pictogram, a car icon represents 20 vehicles. What does half an icon represent?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"10\", \"5\", \"15\", \"2\"]','10','1/2 of 20 = 10.','1/2 of 20 = 10.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1063,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','The table shows sales: Mon 10, Tue 15, Wed 20, Thu 25, Fri 30. What was the average daily sales?','The table shows sales: Mon 10, Tue 15, Wed 20, Thu 25, Fri 30. What was the average daily sales?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"20\", \"22\", \"25\", \"18\"]','20','Sum = 100. 100 ÷ 5 = 20.','Sum = 100. 100 ÷ 5 = 20.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1064,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','A spinner has 8 equal sections numbered 1 to 8. What is the probability of landing on a number greater than 5?','A spinner has 8 equal sections numbered 1 to 8. What is the probability of landing on a number greater than 5?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"3/8\", \"1/2\", \"5/8\", \"1/4\"]','3/8','Numbers greater than 5: 6, 7, 8 (3 sections out of 8) -> 3/8.','Numbers greater than 5: 6, 7, 8 (3 sections out of 8) -> 3/8.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1065,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','If the range of a dataset is 25 and the lowest value is 14, what is the highest value?','If the range of a dataset is 25 and the lowest value is 14, what is the highest value?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"39\", \"40\", \"38\", \"37\"]','39','Highest = Lowest + Range = 14 + 25 = 39.','Highest = Lowest + Range = 14 + 25 = 39.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1066,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a line graph, an upward slope from left to right indicates:','In a line graph, an upward slope from left to right indicates:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"An increase\", \"A decrease\", \"No change\", \"Zero value\"]','An increase','An upward slope indicates that the value is increasing over time.','An upward slope indicates that the value is increasing over time.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1067,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','The average age of a mother and daughter is 24 years. If the mother is 38 years old, how old is the daughter?','The average age of a mother and daughter is 24 years. If the mother is 38 years old, how old is the daughter?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"10 years\", \"12 years\", \"14 years\", \"8 years\"]','10 years','Total age = 24 × 2 = 48 years. Daughter = 48 - 38 = 10 years.','Total age = 24 × 2 = 48 years. Daughter = 48 - 38 = 10 years.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1068,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','Which measurement represents the most frequent value in a dataset?','Which measurement represents the most frequent value in a dataset?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mode\", \"Mean\", \"Median\", \"Range\"]','Mode','The mode is the value that occurs most often.','The mode is the value that occurs most often.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1069,'psr_math_data_probability','psr_maths','In a pie chart with 3 sectors, Sector A is 120° and Sector B is 150°. What is the angle of Sector C?','In a pie chart with 3 sectors, Sector A is 120° and Sector B is 150°. What is the angle of Sector C?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"90°\", \"80°\", \"100°\", \"75°\"]','90°','Total angle = 360°. Sector C = 360 - (120 + 150) = 360 - 270 = 90°.','Total angle = 360°. Sector C = 360 - (120 + 150) = 360 - 270 = 90°.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1070,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which organ acts as the main muscular pump in the human circulatory system?','Which organ acts as the main muscular pump in the human circulatory system?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Heart\", \"Lungs\", \"Brain\", \"Liver\"]','Heart','The heart pumps oxygenated and deoxygenated blood throughout the human body.','The heart pumps oxygenated and deoxygenated blood throughout the human body.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1071,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which blood vessels carry blood AWAY from the heart under high pressure?','Which blood vessels carry blood AWAY from the heart under high pressure?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Arteries\", \"Veins\", \"Capillaries\", \"Valves\"]','Arteries','Arteries carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart to body tissues (Remember: A for Away).','Arteries carry oxygen-rich blood away from the heart to body tissues (Remember: A for Away).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1072,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Where does gas exchange take place inside the human lungs?','Where does gas exchange take place inside the human lungs?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Alveoli\", \"Trachea\", \"Bronchi\", \"Diaphragm\"]','Alveoli','Alveoli are tiny air sacs in the lungs with thin walls where oxygen enters blood and carbon dioxide leaves.','Alveoli are tiny air sacs in the lungs with thin walls where oxygen enters blood and carbon dioxide leaves.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1073,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What gas is absorbed into the blood during inhalation?','What gas is absorbed into the blood during inhalation?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Methane\"]','Oxygen','During inhalation, fresh oxygen from the air diffuses across the alveoli into the red blood cells.','During inhalation, fresh oxygen from the air diffuses across the alveoli into the red blood cells.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1074,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What is the main function of red blood cells?','What is the main function of red blood cells?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Transport oxygen\", \"Fight infections\", \"Clot wounds\", \"Digest food\"]','Transport oxygen','Red blood cells contain hemoglobin which binds with oxygen and delivers it to body cells.','Red blood cells contain hemoglobin which binds with oxygen and delivers it to body cells.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1075,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which organ in the digestive system produces bile to break down fats?','Which organ in the digestive system produces bile to break down fats?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Liver\", \"Stomach\", \"Pancreas\", \"Gall bladder\"]','Liver','The liver produces bile, which is stored in the gall bladder and emulsifies fats in the small intestine.','The liver produces bile, which is stored in the gall bladder and emulsifies fats in the small intestine.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1076,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Where is most water reabsorbed from undigested food in the digestive system?','Where is most water reabsorbed from undigested food in the digestive system?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Large intestine\", \"Small intestine\", \"Stomach\", \"Esophagus\"]','Large intestine','The large intestine (colon) reabsorbs water and mineral salts, forming solid feces.','The large intestine (colon) reabsorbs water and mineral salts, forming solid feces.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1077,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What happens to the human diaphragm during inhalation?','What happens to the human diaphragm during inhalation?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It contracts and moves downward\", \"It relaxes and moves upward\", \"It remains stationary\", \"It expands outward\"]','It contracts and moves downward','When inhaling, the diaphragm contracts and flattens downward, expanding chest volume and lowering pressure to draw air in.','When inhaling, the diaphragm contracts and flattens downward, expanding chest volume and lowering pressure to draw air in.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1078,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which component of human blood helps to clot wounds and stop bleeding?','Which component of human blood helps to clot wounds and stop bleeding?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Platelets\", \"Red blood cells\", \"White blood cells\", \"Plasma\"]','Platelets','Platelets form sticky clots at wound sites to prevent excessive blood loss.','Platelets form sticky clots at wound sites to prevent excessive blood loss.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1079,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What is the function of the skeletal system?','What is the function of the skeletal system?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Provide body shape, protect organs and allow movement\", \"Pump blood to muscles\", \"Filter wastes from kidneys\", \"Absorb digested food\"]','Provide body shape, protect organs and allow movement','Bones provide framework, support, protect vital organs like the brain and lungs, and anchor muscles.','Bones provide framework, support, protect vital organs like the brain and lungs, and anchor muscles.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1080,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which joint allows 360-degree rotational movement in all directions?','Which joint allows 360-degree rotational movement in all directions?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ball and socket joint\", \"Hinge joint\", \"Fixed joint\", \"Pivot joint\"]','Ball and socket joint','The shoulder and hip are ball and socket joints allowing rotational movement in multiple planes.','The shoulder and hip are ball and socket joints allowing rotational movement in multiple planes.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1081,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Where does the chemical digestion of food begin?','Where does the chemical digestion of food begin?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mouth\", \"Stomach\", \"Small intestine\", \"Esophagus\"]','Mouth','Saliva contains the enzyme amylase, which begins breaking down starches in the mouth.','Saliva contains the enzyme amylase, which begins breaking down starches in the mouth.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1082,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What organ filters urea and excess salts from the bloodstream to form urine?','What organ filters urea and excess salts from the bloodstream to form urine?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kidneys\", \"Lungs\", \"Liver\", \"Bladder\"]','Kidneys','Kidneys filter blood, remove waste products (urea), and regulate water balance.','Kidneys filter blood, remove waste products (urea), and regulate water balance.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1083,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which blood vessels have thin walls and valves to prevent the backflow of blood?','Which blood vessels have thin walls and valves to prevent the backflow of blood?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Veins\", \"Arteries\", \"Capillaries\", \"Aorta\"]','Veins','Veins carry low-pressure blood back to the heart and contain pocket valves to prevent backward flow.','Veins carry low-pressure blood back to the heart and contain pocket valves to prevent backward flow.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1084,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What connects bone to bone at a joint?','What connects bone to bone at a joint?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ligaments\", \"Tendons\", \"Cartilage\", \"Muscles\"]','Ligaments','Ligaments connect bone to bone, while tendons connect muscle to bone.','Ligaments connect bone to bone, while tendons connect muscle to bone.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1085,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What is the pulse rate of a healthy resting human child typically?','What is the pulse rate of a healthy resting human child typically?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"70 - 100 beats per minute\", \"30 - 40 beats per minute\", \"150 - 200 beats per minute\", \"10 - 20 beats per minute\"]','70 - 100 beats per minute','Resting heart rate in primary school children is usually between 70 and 100 bpm.','Resting heart rate in primary school children is usually between 70 and 100 bpm.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1086,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Why does our breathing rate increase during vigorous exercise?','Why does our breathing rate increase during vigorous exercise?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To supply more oxygen to muscles and remove excess carbon dioxide\", \"To cool down the brain\", \"To rest the lungs\", \"To stop perspiration\"]','To supply more oxygen to muscles and remove excess carbon dioxide','Working muscle cells consume oxygen rapidly for energy and produce more carbon dioxide, triggering faster respiration.','Working muscle cells consume oxygen rapidly for energy and produce more carbon dioxide, triggering faster respiration.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1087,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which organ stores urine before it is excreted from the body?','Which organ stores urine before it is excreted from the body?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Urinary bladder\", \"Kidney\", \"Gallbladder\", \"Urethra\"]','Urinary bladder','The bladder is a muscular sac that stores urine until urination.','The bladder is a muscular sac that stores urine until urination.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1088,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What substance in saliva begins the breakdown of carbohydrates?','What substance in saliva begins the breakdown of carbohydrates?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Salivary amylase\", \"Hydrochloric acid\", \"Pepsin\", \"Bile\"]','Salivary amylase','Amylase breaks complex starch down into simpler sugars (maltose).','Amylase breaks complex starch down into simpler sugars (maltose).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1089,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which bone protects the human brain from injury?','Which bone protects the human brain from injury?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Cranium (Skull)\", \"Rib cage\", \"Pelvis\", \"Femur\"]','Cranium (Skull)','The cranium is a hard bony case protecting the delicate brain tissue.','The cranium is a hard bony case protecting the delicate brain tissue.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1090,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What type of blood is carried by the pulmonary vein from lungs to heart?','What type of blood is carried by the pulmonary vein from lungs to heart?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Oxygenated blood\", \"Deoxygenated blood\", \"Nutrient-free blood\", \"Waste blood\"]','Oxygenated blood','The pulmonary vein is an exception: it brings freshly oxygenated blood from lungs back to the left atrium of the heart.','The pulmonary vein is an exception: it brings freshly oxygenated blood from lungs back to the left atrium of the heart.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1091,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What is the function of the human ribcage?','What is the function of the human ribcage?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Protect the heart and lungs\", \"Help the kidneys filter water\", \"Digest food\", \"Support the spinal cord\"]','Protect the heart and lungs','The 12 pairs of ribs form a cage guarding the vital heart and lungs inside the thorax.','The 12 pairs of ribs form a cage guarding the vital heart and lungs inside the thorax.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1092,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which part of the digestive tract absorbs digested nutrients into the bloodstream?','Which part of the digestive tract absorbs digested nutrients into the bloodstream?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Small intestine\", \"Stomach\", \"Large intestine\", \"Rectum\"]','Small intestine','The inner lining of the small intestine is covered in tiny villi that absorb nutrients into capillaries.','The inner lining of the small intestine is covered in tiny villi that absorb nutrients into capillaries.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1093,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What involuntary wave of muscular contraction pushes food down the esophagus?','What involuntary wave of muscular contraction pushes food down the esophagus?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Peristalsis\", \"Respiration\", \"Circulation\", \"Osmosis\"]','Peristalsis','Peristalsis consists of rhythmic muscle contractions that push food boluses down the digestive tract.','Peristalsis consists of rhythmic muscle contractions that push food boluses down the digestive tract.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1094,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which white blood cells function primarily to destroy harmful pathogens and bacteria?','Which white blood cells function primarily to destroy harmful pathogens and bacteria?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Phagocytes and Lymphocytes\", \"Red blood cells\", \"Platelets\", \"Plasma\"]','Phagocytes and Lymphocytes','White blood cells engulf bacteria and produce antibodies to fight infection.','White blood cells engulf bacteria and produce antibodies to fight infection.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1095,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What happens to pulse rate immediately after running 100 meters?','What happens to pulse rate immediately after running 100 meters?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It increases significantly\", \"It decreases\", \"It drops to zero\", \"It remains exactly the same\"]','It increases significantly','The heart pumps faster to deliver oxygen to exhausted muscles.','The heart pumps faster to deliver oxygen to exhausted muscles.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1096,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which mineral is essential for building strong bones and teeth?','Which mineral is essential for building strong bones and teeth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Calcium\", \"Iron\", \"Iodine\", \"Sodium\"]','Calcium','Calcium and vitamin D are crucial for bone density and healthy teeth.','Calcium and vitamin D are crucial for bone density and healthy teeth.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1097,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which blood vessel carries blood from the right ventricle to the lungs?','Which blood vessel carries blood from the right ventricle to the lungs?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Pulmonary artery\", \"Aorta\", \"Vena cava\", \"Pulmonary vein\"]','Pulmonary artery','The pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle into the lungs for re-oxygenation.','The pulmonary artery carries deoxygenated blood from the right ventricle into the lungs for re-oxygenation.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1098,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','Which part of the skeletal system protects the spinal cord?','Which part of the skeletal system protects the spinal cord?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Vertebral column (Spine)\", \"Femur\", \"Clavicle\", \"Sternum\"]','Vertebral column (Spine)','The backbone consists of 33 vertebrae enclosing and safeguarding the spinal cord.','The backbone consists of 33 vertebrae enclosing and safeguarding the spinal cord.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1099,'psr_sci_human_body','psr_science','What is the role of hydrochloric acid in the stomach?','What is the role of hydrochloric acid in the stomach?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kill ingested bacteria and provide acidic pH for enzymes\", \"Absorb water\", \"Produce bile\", \"Store fats\"]','Kill ingested bacteria and provide acidic pH for enzymes','Stomach acid (pH 1.5 - 2) destroys harmful microbes and activates pepsin to digest proteins.','Stomach acid (pH 1.5 - 2) destroys harmful microbes and activates pepsin to digest proteins.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1100,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What green pigment in plant leaves absorbs sunlight for photosynthesis?','What green pigment in plant leaves absorbs sunlight for photosynthesis?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Chlorophyll\", \"Hemoglobin\", \"Carotene\", \"Melanin\"]','Chlorophyll','Chlorophyll in chloroplasts traps sunlight energy required to convert CO₂ and water into glucose.','Chlorophyll in chloroplasts traps sunlight energy required to convert CO₂ and water into glucose.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1101,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What are the raw materials required for photosynthesis?','What are the raw materials required for photosynthesis?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Carbon dioxide and water\", \"Oxygen and glucose\", \"Nitrogen and soil\", \"Water and oxygen\"]','Carbon dioxide and water','Plants take in carbon dioxide from air and water from roots in the presence of sunlight.','Plants take in carbon dioxide from air and water from roots in the presence of sunlight.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1102,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What gas is released by green plants as a byproduct of photosynthesis?','What gas is released by green plants as a byproduct of photosynthesis?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Hydrogen\"]','Oxygen','Photosynthesis produces glucose and releases vital oxygen into the atmosphere.','Photosynthesis produces glucose and releases vital oxygen into the atmosphere.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1103,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which plant vascular tissue transports water and minerals upward from roots to leaves?','Which plant vascular tissue transports water and minerals upward from roots to leaves?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Xylem\", \"Phloem\", \"Stomata\", \"Pith\"]','Xylem','Xylem vessels conduct water and dissolved minerals from roots up the stem to leaves (Remember: Xylem = Water).','Xylem vessels conduct water and dissolved minerals from roots up the stem to leaves (Remember: Xylem = Water).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1104,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which plant tissue transports manufactured food (sugar) from leaves to all plant parts?','Which plant tissue transports manufactured food (sugar) from leaves to all plant parts?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Phloem\", \"Xylem\", \"Cuticle\", \"Cortex\"]','Phloem','Phloem transports glucose/sucrose made in leaves to growing shoots and storage roots (Remember: Phloem = Food).','Phloem transports glucose/sucrose made in leaves to growing shoots and storage roots (Remember: Phloem = Food).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1105,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Through which microscopic openings in leaves do gases enter and leave?','Through which microscopic openings in leaves do gases enter and leave?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Stomata\", \"Veins\", \"Petioles\", \"Sepals\"]','Stomata','Stomata on the underside of leaves open and close to regulate gas exchange and transpiration.','Stomata on the underside of leaves open and close to regulate gas exchange and transpiration.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1106,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What is the transfer of pollen grains from anther to stigma called?','What is the transfer of pollen grains from anther to stigma called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Pollination\", \"Fertilization\", \"Germination\", \"Dispersal\"]','Pollination','Pollination is the transfer of pollen from the male anther to the female stigma of a flower.','Pollination is the transfer of pollen from the male anther to the female stigma of a flower.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1107,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which part of a flower develops into a fruit after fertilization?','Which part of a flower develops into a fruit after fertilization?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ovary\", \"Petal\", \"Stigma\", \"Anther\"]','Ovary','After fertilization, the ovary swells to become the fruit, while the ovules inside become seeds.','After fertilization, the ovary swells to become the fruit, while the ovules inside become seeds.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1108,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which seed dispersal method is used by fruits with fibrous, water-resistant husks like coconuts?','Which seed dispersal method is used by fruits with fibrous, water-resistant husks like coconuts?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Water dispersal\", \"Wind dispersal\", \"Animal dispersal\", \"Explosive mechanism\"]','Water dispersal','Coconuts and nipah fruits float on sea currents to reach new shores.','Coconuts and nipah fruits float on sea currents to reach new shores.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1109,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What conditions are strictly necessary for seed germination?','What conditions are strictly necessary for seed germination?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Water, Oxygen, and Warmth (WOW)\", \"Sunlight, Soil, and Fertilizer\", \"Water, Darkness, and Wind\", \"Oxygen, Carbon dioxide, and Cold\"]','Water, Oxygen, and Warmth (WOW)','Seeds do not need sunlight or soil to germinate; they need Water, Oxygen, and Warmth (WOW).','Seeds do not need sunlight or soil to germinate; they need Water, Oxygen, and Warmth (WOW).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1110,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which feature is typical of wind-pollinated flowers?','Which feature is typical of wind-pollinated flowers?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Dull petals, no scent, feathery stigmas and light pollen\", \"Large brightly coloured petals with sweet nectar\", \"Strong fragrant scent to attract bees\", \"Sticky pollen and sweet fruits\"]','Dull petals, no scent, feathery stigmas and light pollen','Wind-pollinated flowers (like grass and maize) don\'t need bright colors; their feathery stigmas catch airborne pollen.','Wind-pollinated flowers (like grass and maize) don\'t need bright colors; their feathery stigmas catch airborne pollen.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1111,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What is the loss of water vapor from the leaves of a plant called?','What is the loss of water vapor from the leaves of a plant called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Transpiration\", \"Condensation\", \"Photosynthesis\", \"Respiration\"]','Transpiration','Transpiration is the evaporation of water from plant leaves through open stomata.','Transpiration is the evaporation of water from plant leaves through open stomata.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1112,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Why do mangrove trees (bakau) in Brunei have breathing roots (pneumatophores)?','Why do mangrove trees (bakau) in Brunei have breathing roots (pneumatophores)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To obtain oxygen in waterlogged, muddy soil\", \"To absorb sunlight underwater\", \"To attract crabs\", \"To prevent leaves from dropping\"]','To obtain oxygen in waterlogged, muddy soil','Pneumatophores grow upward above the oxygen-poor mangrove mud to take in atmospheric air.','Pneumatophores grow upward above the oxygen-poor mangrove mud to take in atmospheric air.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1113,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which part of a seed provides nourishment for the growing embryo during germination?','Which part of a seed provides nourishment for the growing embryo during germination?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Cotyledon (seed leaf)\", \"Seed coat (testa)\", \"Radicle\", \"Micropyle\"]','Cotyledon (seed leaf)','The cotyledon stores starch and proteins that nourish the seedling until green leaves develop.','The cotyledon stores starch and proteins that nourish the seedling until green leaves develop.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1114,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What structure emerges first from a germinating seed?','What structure emerges first from a germinating seed?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Radicle (root)\", \"Plumule (shoot)\", \"First leaf\", \"Flower\"]','Radicle (root)','The radicle emerges first to anchor the seedling and absorb moisture from the soil.','The radicle emerges first to anchor the seedling and absorb moisture from the soil.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1115,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','In a food chain, what role do green plants always play?','In a food chain, what role do green plants always play?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Producers\", \"Primary consumers\", \"Decomposers\", \"Predators\"]','Producers','Plants produce their own food through photosynthesis and form the base of food chains.','Plants produce their own food through photosynthesis and form the base of food chains.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1116,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which plant responds to touch by rapidly folding its leaves?','Which plant responds to touch by rapidly folding its leaves?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mimosa pudica (Touch-me-not)\", \"Hibiscus\", \"Fern\", \"Orchid\"]','Mimosa pudica (Touch-me-not)','Mimosa leaves fold when touched due to changes in turgor pressure at the leaf base.','Mimosa leaves fold when touched due to changes in turgor pressure at the leaf base.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1117,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What is the female reproductive part of a flower called?','What is the female reproductive part of a flower called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Carpel / Pistil\", \"Stamen\", \"Anther\", \"Filament\"]','Carpel / Pistil','The pistil comprises stigma, style, and ovary. The male part is the stamen (anther and filament).','The pistil comprises stigma, style, and ovary. The male part is the stamen (anther and filament).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1118,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','How are dandelion and angsana seeds dispersed?','How are dandelion and angsana seeds dispersed?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"By wind\", \"By water\", \"By animal fur\", \"By explosive split\"]','By wind','They have parachute-like hairs or wing-like blades that allow wind to carry them away.','They have parachute-like hairs or wing-like blades that allow wind to carry them away.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1119,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which test proves that starch is present in a green leaf?','Which test proves that starch is present in a green leaf?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Iodine solution turns blue-black\", \"Benedict solution turns red\", \"Limewater turns milky\", \"Biuret solution turns purple\"]','Iodine solution turns blue-black','Iodine solution changes from yellow-brown to dark blue-black in the presence of starch.','Iodine solution changes from yellow-brown to dark blue-black in the presence of starch.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1120,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Why must a leaf be boiled in alcohol before testing for starch?','Why must a leaf be boiled in alcohol before testing for starch?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To remove chlorophyll so color change can be seen\", \"To add starch\", \"To soften the stems\", \"To kill bacteria\"]','To remove chlorophyll so color change can be seen','Alcohol dissolves the green chlorophyll, bleaching the leaf white so iodine color change is clear.','Alcohol dissolves the green chlorophyll, bleaching the leaf white so iodine color change is clear.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1121,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What happens to plant stomata during severe hot droughts?','What happens to plant stomata during severe hot droughts?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"They close to conserve water\", \"They open wider to absorb heat\", \"They disappear\", \"They release all moisture\"]','They close to conserve water','Guard cells lose turgidity and close stomata to minimize water loss through transpiration.','Guard cells lose turgidity and close stomata to minimize water loss through transpiration.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1122,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which seed dispersal method is used by rambutan and mango?','Which seed dispersal method is used by rambutan and mango?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Animal dispersal (eaten and seeds discarded)\", \"Wind dispersal\", \"Water currents\", \"Explosive pod\"]','Animal dispersal (eaten and seeds discarded)','Animals and humans eat the sweet fleshy fruit and drop the seeds elsewhere.','Animals and humans eat the sweet fleshy fruit and drop the seeds elsewhere.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1123,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What gas do plants take in during nighttime respiration?','What gas do plants take in during nighttime respiration?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Oxygen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Nitrogen\", \"Chlorine\"]','Oxygen','At night without sunlight, photosynthesis stops and plants only respire, taking in oxygen and giving out CO₂.','At night without sunlight, photosynthesis stops and plants only respire, taking in oxygen and giving out CO₂.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1124,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What type of root system does a maize (corn) plant have?','What type of root system does a maize (corn) plant have?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Fibrous root system\", \"Taproot system\", \"Aerial root system\", \"Tuber root system\"]','Fibrous root system','Monocots like maize and grass have a cluster of fibrous roots rather than one deep central taproot.','Monocots like maize and grass have a cluster of fibrous roots rather than one deep central taproot.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1125,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','How does the cactus plant adapt to desert conditions?','How does the cactus plant adapt to desert conditions?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Leaves reduced to spines and thick fleshy stem to store water\", \"Broad thin leaves to catch rain\", \"No roots\", \"Soft hollow stem\"]','Leaves reduced to spines and thick fleshy stem to store water','Spines minimize transpiration loss, while thick succulent stems store water and photosynthesize.','Spines minimize transpiration loss, while thick succulent stems store water and photosynthesize.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1126,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What is an organism that breaks down dead plants and animals called?','What is an organism that breaks down dead plants and animals called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Decomposer (Fungi and Bacteria)\", \"Carnivore\", \"Herbivore\", \"Parasite\"]','Decomposer (Fungi and Bacteria)','Decomposers recycle nutrients from dead organic matter back into the soil.','Decomposers recycle nutrients from dead organic matter back into the soil.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1127,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which part of a flower produces pollen grains?','Which part of a flower produces pollen grains?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Anther\", \"Stigma\", \"Filament\", \"Ovary\"]','Anther','The anther sits atop the filament and contains pollen sacs that produce pollen.','The anther sits atop the filament and contains pollen sacs that produce pollen.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1128,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','What type of relationship exists when an orchid grows on a tree trunk without harming it?','What type of relationship exists when an orchid grows on a tree trunk without harming it?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Commensalism (Epiphyte)\", \"Parasitism\", \"Predation\", \"Mutualism\"]','Commensalism (Epiphyte)','The orchid gains high sunlight exposure without stealing nutrients from the host tree.','The orchid gains high sunlight exposure without stealing nutrients from the host tree.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1129,'psr_sci_plants_living_things','psr_science','Which of the following plants reproduces via spores rather than seeds?','Which of the following plants reproduces via spores rather than seeds?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Bird\'s nest fern\", \"Hibiscus\", \"Papaya\", \"Sunflower\"]','Bird\'s nest fern','Ferns and mosses are non-flowering plants that reproduce using microscopic spores on the underside of fronds.','Ferns and mosses are non-flowering plants that reproduce using microscopic spores on the underside of fronds.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1130,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What is the primary source of light and heat energy for planet Earth?','What is the primary source of light and heat energy for planet Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The Sun\", \"The Moon\", \"Coal fires\", \"Volcanoes\"]','The Sun','Solar energy from the Sun powers the water cycle, weather, and plant photosynthesis on Earth.','Solar energy from the Sun powers the water cycle, weather, and plant photosynthesis on Earth.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1131,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which of the following is a non-renewable source of energy?','Which of the following is a non-renewable source of energy?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Petroleum\", \"Solar energy\", \"Wind power\", \"Biomass\"]','Petroleum','Fossil fuels (petroleum, coal, natural gas) take millions of years to form and will eventually deplete.','Fossil fuels (petroleum, coal, natural gas) take millions of years to form and will eventually deplete.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1132,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What energy transformation occurs when an electric iron is switched on?','What energy transformation occurs when an electric iron is switched on?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Electrical energy to Heat energy\", \"Chemical energy to Light energy\", \"Kinetic energy to Sound energy\", \"Heat energy to Potential energy\"]','Electrical energy to Heat energy','Electrical current heating the heating element converts electrical energy into thermal heat energy.','Electrical current heating the heating element converts electrical energy into thermal heat energy.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1133,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','In a torchlight, what energy change takes place when it is turned on?','In a torchlight, what energy change takes place when it is turned on?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Chemical -> Electrical -> Light + Heat\", \"Kinetic -> Sound -> Light\", \"Heat -> Electrical -> Sound\", \"Potential -> Nuclear -> Light\"]','Chemical -> Electrical -> Light + Heat','Chemical energy in dry cells converts into electrical current, then into light and heat in the bulb filament.','Chemical energy in dry cells converts into electrical current, then into light and heat in the bulb filament.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1134,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What component in an electrical circuit opens or closes the pathway for current flow?','What component in an electrical circuit opens or closes the pathway for current flow?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Switch\", \"Battery\", \"Bulb\", \"Connecting wire\"]','Switch','A switch allows current to flow when closed and interrupts current flow when opened.','A switch allows current to flow when closed and interrupts current flow when opened.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1135,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What happens in a series circuit if one bulb blows out (filament breaks)?','What happens in a series circuit if one bulb blows out (filament breaks)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"All other bulbs turn off\", \"Other bulbs become brighter\", \"Other bulbs stay on unchanged\", \"The circuit starts a fire\"]','All other bulbs turn off','In a series circuit, there is only one single path; if any component breaks, the whole circuit is broken.','In a series circuit, there is only one single path; if any component breaks, the whole circuit is broken.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1136,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Why are house lights connected in parallel circuits rather than in series?','Why are house lights connected in parallel circuits rather than in series?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Each appliance can be operated independently and receives full voltage\", \"It saves all electricity\", \"Parallel circuits use no switches\", \"Parallel circuits prevent all bulbs from lighting\"]','Each appliance can be operated independently and receives full voltage','In parallel, if one bulb burns out, others continue working normally.','In parallel, if one bulb burns out, others continue working normally.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1137,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which of the following materials is a good conductor of electricity?','Which of the following materials is a good conductor of electricity?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Copper wire\", \"Rubber glove\", \"Plastic ruler\", \"Dry wooden stick\"]','Copper wire','Metals like copper, silver, and aluminum allow electric charges to pass through freely.','Metals like copper, silver, and aluminum allow electric charges to pass through freely.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1138,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Why are electric cables coated with plastic or rubber?','Why are electric cables coated with plastic or rubber?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Because rubber is an insulator that prevents electric shocks\", \"Because plastic conducts electricity faster\", \"To make cables heavier\", \"To change the current color\"]','Because rubber is an insulator that prevents electric shocks','Insulators have high resistance and block current flow, protecting users from live wire shocks.','Insulators have high resistance and block current flow, protecting users from live wire shocks.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1139,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which instrument is used to measure electrical current in a circuit?','Which instrument is used to measure electrical current in a circuit?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ammeter\", \"Voltmeter\", \"Thermometer\", \"Barometer\"]','Ammeter','An ammeter measures electric current in amperes (A).','An ammeter measures electric current in amperes (A).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1140,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What type of energy is stored in food, fuel, and batteries?','What type of energy is stored in food, fuel, and batteries?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Chemical potential energy\", \"Kinetic energy\", \"Light energy\", \"Sound energy\"]','Chemical potential energy','Chemical potential energy is stored in molecular bonds and released during chemical reactions.','Chemical potential energy is stored in molecular bonds and released during chemical reactions.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1141,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','A roller coaster car at the very top of a tall hill possesses maximum:','A roller coaster car at the very top of a tall hill possesses maximum:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Gravitational potential energy\", \"Kinetic energy\", \"Sound energy\", \"Thermal energy\"]','Gravitational potential energy','Gravitational potential energy depends on height and mass (PE = mgh).','Gravitational potential energy depends on height and mass (PE = mgh).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1142,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','As the roller coaster car plunges down the hill, its potential energy transforms into:','As the roller coaster car plunges down the hill, its potential energy transforms into:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kinetic energy\", \"Chemical energy\", \"Nuclear energy\", \"Electrical energy\"]','Kinetic energy','Loss of height leads to acceleration and gain of kinetic (motion) energy.','Loss of height leads to acceleration and gain of kinetic (motion) energy.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1143,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which renewable energy resource harnesses the natural heat from inside the Earth?','Which renewable energy resource harnesses the natural heat from inside the Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Geothermal energy\", \"Hydroelectric energy\", \"Wind energy\", \"Tidal energy\"]','Geothermal energy','Geothermal energy utilizes underground steam and volcanic heat to drive turbines.','Geothermal energy utilizes underground steam and volcanic heat to drive turbines.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1144,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What happens to the brightness of two identical bulbs connected in series if a third bulb is added?','What happens to the brightness of two identical bulbs connected in series if a third bulb is added?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The bulbs become dimmer\", \"The bulbs become brighter\", \"The brightness remains unchanged\", \"The bulbs explode\"]','The bulbs become dimmer','Adding bulbs in series increases total circuit resistance, decreasing current and sharing voltage.','Adding bulbs in series increases total circuit resistance, decreasing current and sharing voltage.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1145,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which energy transformation occurs in a hydroelectric power station (dam)?','Which energy transformation occurs in a hydroelectric power station (dam)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Gravitational PE -> Kinetic -> Electrical energy\", \"Chemical -> Heat -> Nuclear\", \"Solar -> Chemical -> Light\", \"Sound -> Kinetic -> Heat\"]','Gravitational PE -> Kinetic -> Electrical energy','Water stored high up flows down through penstocks (kinetic), turning turbine generators (electrical).','Water stored high up flows down through penstocks (kinetic), turning turbine generators (electrical).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1146,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What will happen if you connect a bulb with a broken filament in an electric circuit?','What will happen if you connect a bulb with a broken filament in an electric circuit?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The circuit will be open and the bulb will not light\", \"The bulb will shine brighter\", \"The wires will freeze\", \"Current will bypass the bulb\"]','The circuit will be open and the bulb will not light','A broken filament creates an open circuit (incomplete loop), preventing current flow.','A broken filament creates an open circuit (incomplete loop), preventing current flow.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1147,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Why should you never touch electrical sockets with wet hands?','Why should you never touch electrical sockets with wet hands?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Water contains ions and conducts electricity, causing severe shock\", \"Water evaporates too quickly\", \"Water damages the plastic cover\", \"Water changes the frequency of light\"]','Water contains ions and conducts electricity, causing severe shock','Tap water is a conductor of electricity; moisture drastically reduces skin resistance.','Tap water is a conductor of electricity; moisture drastically reduces skin resistance.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1148,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What safety device contains a thin wire that melts when current exceeds a safe limit?','What safety device contains a thin wire that melts when current exceeds a safe limit?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Fuse\", \"Battery\", \"Switch\", \"Transformer\"]','Fuse','A fuse breaks the circuit if dangerous power surges occur, preventing electrical fires.','A fuse breaks the circuit if dangerous power surges occur, preventing electrical fires.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1149,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which of the following is an example of kinetic energy?','Which of the following is an example of kinetic energy?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"A speeding bullet train\", \"A stretched rubber band\", \"A battery on a shelf\", \"A boulder resting on a cliff\"]','A speeding bullet train','Kinetic energy is the energy possessed by moving objects.','Kinetic energy is the energy possessed by moving objects.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1150,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','A solar cell (photovoltaic panel) converts:','A solar cell (photovoltaic panel) converts:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Light energy directly into Electrical energy\", \"Heat energy into Chemical energy\", \"Sound energy into Motion\", \"Kinetic energy into Nuclear energy\"]','Light energy directly into Electrical energy','Photovoltaic cells use semiconductor materials to convert solar photons into electricity.','Photovoltaic cells use semiconductor materials to convert solar photons into electricity.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1151,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What type of energy is stored in a compressed or stretched spring?','What type of energy is stored in a compressed or stretched spring?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Elastic potential energy\", \"Kinetic energy\", \"Chemical energy\", \"Thermal energy\"]','Elastic potential energy','Deforming an elastic object stores elastic potential energy that returns when released.','Deforming an elastic object stores elastic potential energy that returns when released.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1152,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What is the standard unit of electrical energy consumed in households?','What is the standard unit of electrical energy consumed in households?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kilowatt-hour (kWh)\", \"Newton\", \"Pascal\", \"Volt\"]','Kilowatt-hour (kWh)','Electricity meters measure energy consumption in kilowatt-hours (kWh).','Electricity meters measure energy consumption in kilowatt-hours (kWh).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1153,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which material would make a bulb in a circuit light up if inserted into a gap?','Which material would make a bulb in a circuit light up if inserted into a gap?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"An iron nail\", \"A glass rod\", \"A wooden pencil\", \"A ceramic tile\"]','An iron nail','Iron is a metal and an electrical conductor, completing the circuit.','Iron is a metal and an electrical conductor, completing the circuit.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1154,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What energy transformation occurs in a microphone?','What energy transformation occurs in a microphone?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Sound energy to Electrical energy\", \"Electrical energy to Sound energy\", \"Light energy to Heat energy\", \"Kinetic energy to Chemical energy\"]','Sound energy to Electrical energy','Sound waves vibrate a diaphragm that generates electrical audio signals.','Sound waves vibrate a diaphragm that generates electrical audio signals.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1155,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What energy transformation occurs in a loudspeaker?','What energy transformation occurs in a loudspeaker?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Electrical energy to Sound energy\", \"Sound energy to Light energy\", \"Chemical energy to Heat energy\", \"Thermal energy to Kinetic energy\"]','Electrical energy to Sound energy','Loudspeakers convert electrical audio impulses back into audible air vibrations.','Loudspeakers convert electrical audio impulses back into audible air vibrations.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1156,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','In which circuit arrangement do all bulbs share the same brightness and independent paths?','In which circuit arrangement do all bulbs share the same brightness and independent paths?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Parallel circuit\", \"Series circuit\", \"Open circuit\", \"Short circuit\"]','Parallel circuit','Parallel branches provide full battery voltage to each bulb independently.','Parallel branches provide full battery voltage to each bulb independently.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1157,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What happens when too many high-power appliances are plugged into one extension socket?','What happens when too many high-power appliances are plugged into one extension socket?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Overloading, causing wires to overheat and risk fire\", \"The appliances freeze\", \"Electricity usage drops to zero\", \"Voltage doubles\"]','Overloading, causing wires to overheat and risk fire','Overloading draws excessive current through thin extension wires, generating extreme heat.','Overloading draws excessive current through thin extension wires, generating extreme heat.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1158,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','Which gas emitted from burning fossil fuels is the primary cause of global warming?','Which gas emitted from burning fossil fuels is the primary cause of global warming?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Carbon dioxide\", \"Oxygen\", \"Argon\", \"Helium\"]','Carbon dioxide','Carbon dioxide traps heat in the atmosphere, creating the enhanced greenhouse effect.','Carbon dioxide traps heat in the atmosphere, creating the enhanced greenhouse effect.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1159,'psr_sci_energy_electricity','psr_science','What energy change occurs when rubbing two cold hands briskly together?','What energy change occurs when rubbing two cold hands briskly together?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kinetic energy converts to Heat energy via friction\", \"Light energy converts to Sound\", \"Chemical energy converts to Nuclear\", \"Potential energy converts to Magnetic\"]','Kinetic energy converts to Heat energy via friction','Mechanical friction converts motion into thermal warmth.','Mechanical friction converts motion into thermal warmth.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1160,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What is a force?','What is a force?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"A push or a pull acting on an object\", \"The speed of a vehicle\", \"The weight of air\", \"The color of an object\"]','A push or a pull acting on an object','A force is defined as a push or a pull that can change an object\'s speed, direction, or shape.','A force is defined as a push or a pull that can change an object\'s speed, direction, or shape.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1161,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What force pulls all dropped objects downward toward the center of the Earth?','What force pulls all dropped objects downward toward the center of the Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Gravity\", \"Friction\", \"Magnetism\", \"Electrostatic force\"]','Gravity','Gravitational force pulls objects with mass towards Earth\'s center.','Gravitational force pulls objects with mass towards Earth\'s center.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1162,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What force opposes the sliding motion between two surfaces in contact?','What force opposes the sliding motion between two surfaces in contact?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Friction\", \"Gravity\", \"Upthrust\", \"Tension\"]','Friction','Friction acts in the direction opposite to motion, slowing down moving surfaces.','Friction acts in the direction opposite to motion, slowing down moving surfaces.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1163,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which of the following helps to reduce friction between moving machine parts?','Which of the following helps to reduce friction between moving machine parts?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Applying lubricating oil or grease\", \"Roughening the metal surfaces\", \"Sprinkling sand on gears\", \"Removing ball bearings\"]','Applying lubricating oil or grease','Lubricants form a smooth liquid film that prevents rough surface peaks from grinding together.','Lubricants form a smooth liquid film that prevents rough surface peaks from grinding together.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1164,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Why do racing car tyres have deep tread patterns on wet tracks?','Why do racing car tyres have deep tread patterns on wet tracks?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To channel water away and increase grip\", \"To make the car lighter\", \"To look attractive\", \"To decrease friction\"]','To channel water away and increase grip','Tread grooves expel rainwater, preventing hydroplaning and maintaining road contact.','Tread grooves expel rainwater, preventing hydroplaning and maintaining road contact.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1165,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which simple machine consists of a rigid bar pivoting around a fixed point (fulcrum)?','Which simple machine consists of a rigid bar pivoting around a fixed point (fulcrum)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Lever\", \"Pulley\", \"Incline plane (Ramp)\", \"Wedge\"]','Lever','A lever rotates around a fulcrum to amplify effort force (e.g. crowbar, scissors, seesaw).','A lever rotates around a fulcrum to amplify effort force (e.g. crowbar, scissors, seesaw).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1166,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','In a wheelbarrow, where is the load located?','In a wheelbarrow, where is the load located?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Between the fulcrum (wheel) and the effort (handles)\", \"At the handles\", \"Under the wheel\", \"Behind the worker\"]','Between the fulcrum (wheel) and the effort (handles)','A wheelbarrow is a Class 2 lever: Fulcrum at wheel, Load in the middle, Effort at handles.','A wheelbarrow is a Class 2 lever: Fulcrum at wheel, Load in the middle, Effort at handles.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1167,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which simple machine is used to easily raise heavy flags to the top of a flagpole?','Which simple machine is used to easily raise heavy flags to the top of a flagpole?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Fixed pulley\", \"Screw\", \"Wedge\", \"Wheel and axle\"]','Fixed pulley','A fixed pulley changes the direction of the applied force: pulling downward raises the flag upward.','A fixed pulley changes the direction of the applied force: pulling downward raises the flag upward.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1168,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','A ramp used to roll heavy barrels into a truck is an example of a:','A ramp used to roll heavy barrels into a truck is an example of a:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Inclined plane\", \"Lever\", \"Wedge\", \"Pulley\"]','Inclined plane','An inclined plane allows heavy loads to be raised using less effort force over a longer distance.','An inclined plane allows heavy loads to be raised using less effort force over a longer distance.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1169,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which simple machine has two inclined planes placed back to back, used for splitting wood?','Which simple machine has two inclined planes placed back to back, used for splitting wood?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Wedge (like an axe)\", \"Screw\", \"Wheel and axle\", \"Pulley\"]','Wedge (like an axe)','An axe or knife is a wedge that concentrates downward force to push materials apart sideways.','An axe or knife is a wedge that concentrates downward force to push materials apart sideways.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1170,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What is the unit used to measure force in science?','What is the unit used to measure force in science?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Newton (N)\", \"Kilogram (kg)\", \"Joule (J)\", \"Watt (W)\"]','Newton (N)','Force is measured in Newtons (N) using a spring balance (dynamometer).','Force is measured in Newtons (N) using a spring balance (dynamometer).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1171,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What effect does friction have on the soles of school shoes over time?','What effect does friction have on the soles of school shoes over time?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It wears them down smooth\", \"It makes them thicker\", \"It turns them into rubber\", \"It has no effect\"]','It wears them down smooth','Friction gradually erodes and wears away rubber shoe treads.','Friction gradually erodes and wears away rubber shoe treads.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1172,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','When an apple falls from a tree, its downward speed increases because of:','When an apple falls from a tree, its downward speed increases because of:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Unbalanced gravitational force\", \"Friction pushing it down\", \"Wind blowing downward\", \"Magnetic attraction\"]','Unbalanced gravitational force','Gravity exerts an unbalanced downward force causing gravitational acceleration.','Gravity exerts an unbalanced downward force causing gravitational acceleration.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1173,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What type of force enables a parachute to slow down a skydiver\'s fall?','What type of force enables a parachute to slow down a skydiver\'s fall?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Air resistance (drag)\", \"Magnetic force\", \"Centrifugal force\", \"Chemical force\"]','Air resistance (drag)','Air resistance is a frictional drag force opposing motion through atmospheric gas.','Air resistance is a frictional drag force opposing motion through atmospheric gas.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1174,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Why do gymnasts apply chalk powder to their hands before performing?','Why do gymnasts apply chalk powder to their hands before performing?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To increase friction and prevent slipping\", \"To make hands slippery\", \"To cool down palms\", \"To reduce skin temperature\"]','To increase friction and prevent slipping','Chalk absorbs sweat and increases friction between palms and the gymnastic bars.','Chalk absorbs sweat and increases friction between palms and the gymnastic bars.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1175,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','A screwdriver turning a screw is an example of which simple machine?','A screwdriver turning a screw is an example of which simple machine?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Wheel and axle\", \"Pulley\", \"Lever\", \"Wedge\"]','Wheel and axle','The wide handle is the wheel and the narrow shaft is the axle, multiplying turning force.','The wide handle is the wheel and the narrow shaft is the axle, multiplying turning force.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1176,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What type of lever has the fulcrum positioned in the center between effort and load?','What type of lever has the fulcrum positioned in the center between effort and load?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Class 1 lever (e.g. Seesaw, Scissors)\", \"Class 2 lever (e.g. Wheelbarrow)\", \"Class 3 lever (e.g. Tweezer)\", \"Class 4 lever\"]','Class 1 lever (e.g. Seesaw, Scissors)','Class 1 levers have the Fulcrum in the middle: Load - Fulcrum - Effort.','Class 1 levers have the Fulcrum in the middle: Load - Fulcrum - Effort.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1177,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which object operates as a Class 3 lever with the effort applied between fulcrum and load?','Which object operates as a Class 3 lever with the effort applied between fulcrum and load?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Tweezers / Fishing rod\", \"Crowbar\", \"Bottle opener\", \"Nutcracker\"]','Tweezers / Fishing rod','Class 3 levers have Effort in the middle, allowing speed and precision rather than force multiplication.','Class 3 levers have Effort in the middle, allowing speed and precision rather than force multiplication.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1178,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What happens to an object when the forces acting upon it are balanced?','What happens to an object when the forces acting upon it are balanced?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It remains stationary or continues moving at constant speed\", \"It accelerates rapidly\", \"It explodes\", \"It changes mass\"]','It remains stationary or continues moving at constant speed','Balanced forces result in zero net force, maintaining equilibrium according to Newton\'s First Law.','Balanced forces result in zero net force, maintaining equilibrium according to Newton\'s First Law.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1179,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Why do airplanes and high-speed trains have streamlined teardrop shapes?','Why do airplanes and high-speed trains have streamlined teardrop shapes?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To reduce air resistance and drag\", \"To make them look like birds\", \"To increase their weight\", \"To increase air friction\"]','To reduce air resistance and drag','Streamlined profiles allow air to flow smoothly around the vehicle with minimal turbulent drag.','Streamlined profiles allow air to flow smoothly around the vehicle with minimal turbulent drag.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1180,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What instrument is commonly used in school science labs to measure pulling force?','What instrument is commonly used in school science labs to measure pulling force?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Spring balance (Newton meter)\", \"Beam balance\", \"Stopwatch\", \"Thermometer\"]','Spring balance (Newton meter)','A spring balance measures force in Newtons based on Hooke\'s Law of spring extension.','A spring balance measures force in Newtons based on Hooke\'s Law of spring extension.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1181,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','If you push a heavy wooden box across a rough carpet vs smooth tiles, on which surface is friction higher?','If you push a heavy wooden box across a rough carpet vs smooth tiles, on which surface is friction higher?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Rough carpet\", \"Smooth tiles\", \"Both are identical\", \"Friction is zero on carpet\"]','Rough carpet','Rough carpet fibers interlock more strongly with the box bottom, generating higher friction.','Rough carpet fibers interlock more strongly with the box bottom, generating higher friction.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1182,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Which simple machine is essentially an inclined plane wrapped spirally around a cylinder?','Which simple machine is essentially an inclined plane wrapped spirally around a cylinder?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Screw\", \"Lever\", \"Pulley\", \"Wedge\"]','Screw','A screw is an inclined plane wrapped around a central core to hold materials firmly together.','A screw is an inclined plane wrapped around a central core to hold materials firmly together.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1183,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What force causes a floating ship to stay afloat on seawater?','What force causes a floating ship to stay afloat on seawater?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Upthrust (Buoyancy force)\", \"Gravity\", \"Friction\", \"Air pressure\"]','Upthrust (Buoyancy force)','The upward buoyant force exerted by displaced water balances the downward gravitational weight of the ship.','The upward buoyant force exerted by displaced water balances the downward gravitational weight of the ship.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1184,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','When two north poles of two bar magnets are pushed towards each other, they will:','When two north poles of two bar magnets are pushed towards each other, they will:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Repel each other\", \"Attract each other\", \"Stick tightly\", \"Neutralize\"]','Repel each other','Like magnetic poles (N-N or S-S) repel; unlike poles (N-S) attract.','Like magnetic poles (N-N or S-S) repel; unlike poles (N-S) attract.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1185,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Why are ball bearings placed inside bicycle wheel hubs?','Why are ball bearings placed inside bicycle wheel hubs?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"To replace sliding friction with rolling friction\", \"To add weight to the wheel\", \"To make the wheel magnetic\", \"To stop the wheel from turning\"]','To replace sliding friction with rolling friction','Rolling friction is far lower than sliding friction, allowing wheels to spin freely.','Rolling friction is far lower than sliding friction, allowing wheels to spin freely.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1186,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','What force acts when a stretched bowstring propels an arrow forward?','What force acts when a stretched bowstring propels an arrow forward?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Elastic force\", \"Gravitational force\", \"Frictional force\", \"Magnetic force\"]','Elastic force','The bent bow restores its original shape, releasing stored elastic energy as propulsive force.','The bent bow restores its original shape, releasing stored elastic energy as propulsive force.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1187,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','If a force of 10 N pushes a toy car to the right and a frictional force of 4 N acts to the left, what is the net force?','If a force of 10 N pushes a toy car to the right and a frictional force of 4 N acts to the left, what is the net force?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"6 N to the right\", \"14 N to the right\", \"6 N to the left\", \"10 N to the left\"]','6 N to the right','Net force = 10 N - 4 N = 6 N in the direction of the push (right).','Net force = 10 N - 4 N = 6 N in the direction of the push (right).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1188,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','Why is walking on ice much more difficult and slippery than on tarmac pavement?','Why is walking on ice much more difficult and slippery than on tarmac pavement?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ice has very little friction\", \"Ice has too much friction\", \"Gravity does not work on ice\", \"Ice is a magnetic insulator\"]','Ice has very little friction','A microscopic water film on smooth ice reduces friction to near zero, causing shoes to slip.','A microscopic water film on smooth ice reduces friction to near zero, causing shoes to slip.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1189,'psr_sci_forces_machines','psr_science','How does using a longer ramp make loading heavy furniture into a van easier?','How does using a longer ramp make loading heavy furniture into a van easier?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It requires less effort force over a longer distance\", \"It reduces the weight of the furniture\", \"It eliminates gravity\", \"It shortens the travel distance\"]','It requires less effort force over a longer distance','A gentler slope reduces the effort required to lift the load.','A gentler slope reduces the effort required to lift the load.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1190,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which state of matter has a definite shape and a definite volume?','Which state of matter has a definite shape and a definite volume?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Solid\", \"Liquid\", \"Gas\", \"Plasma\"]','Solid','Solids have tightly packed particles vibrating in fixed positions, maintaining constant shape and volume.','Solids have tightly packed particles vibrating in fixed positions, maintaining constant shape and volume.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1191,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which state of matter has a definite volume but takes the shape of its container?','Which state of matter has a definite volume but takes the shape of its container?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Liquid\", \"Solid\", \"Gas\", \"Vapour\"]','Liquid','Liquids flow to match container shape because particles can slide over one another.','Liquids flow to match container shape because particles can slide over one another.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1192,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is the process of a liquid turning into a gas at its boiling point throughout the liquid called?','What is the process of a liquid turning into a gas at its boiling point throughout the liquid called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Boiling\", \"Evaporation\", \"Condensation\", \"Freezing\"]','Boiling','Boiling occurs at a fixed temperature (100°C for pure water) with bubbles forming throughout.','Boiling occurs at a fixed temperature (100°C for pure water) with bubbles forming throughout.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1193,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is the change of state from gas to liquid called?','What is the change of state from gas to liquid called?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Condensation\", \"Evaporation\", \"Melting\", \"Sublimation\"]','Condensation','Condensation occurs when warm gas cools, losing kinetic energy and becoming liquid droplets.','Condensation occurs when warm gas cools, losing kinetic energy and becoming liquid droplets.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1194,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','At what temperature does pure water freeze into ice under normal atmospheric pressure?','At what temperature does pure water freeze into ice under normal atmospheric pressure?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"0°C\", \"100°C\", \"32°C\", \"-10°C\"]','0°C','The freezing/melting point of pure water is 0°C; its boiling point is 100°C.','The freezing/melting point of pure water is 0°C; its boiling point is 100°C.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1195,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What causes day and night on Earth?','What causes day and night on Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Earth\'s rotation on its own axis every 24 hours\", \"Earth\'s revolution around the Sun every 365 days\", \"The Moon blocking the Sun\", \"The Sun rotating around the Earth\"]','Earth\'s rotation on its own axis every 24 hours','As Earth rotates from West to East, the side facing the Sun experiences day, while the opposite side experiences night.','As Earth rotates from West to East, the side facing the Sun experiences day, while the opposite side experiences night.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1196,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','How long does it take for Earth to complete one full revolution around the Sun?','How long does it take for Earth to complete one full revolution around the Sun?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"365 1/4 days (1 year)\", \"24 hours\", \"30 days\", \"28 days\"]','365 1/4 days (1 year)','One complete orbit around the Sun takes approximately 365.25 days.','One complete orbit around the Sun takes approximately 365.25 days.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1197,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Why does the Moon appear to shine in the night sky?','Why does the Moon appear to shine in the night sky?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"It reflects light from the Sun\", \"It produces its own light like a star\", \"It absorbs city lights\", \"It is made of glowing gas\"]','It reflects light from the Sun','The Moon has no luminous light source of its own; it reflects solar rays back to Earth.','The Moon has no luminous light source of its own; it reflects solar rays back to Earth.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1198,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which planet is closest to the Sun in our solar system?','Which planet is closest to the Sun in our solar system?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mercury\", \"Venus\", \"Mars\", \"Earth\"]','Mercury','Mercury is the first and smallest planet orbiting nearest to the Sun.','Mercury is the first and smallest planet orbiting nearest to the Sun.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1199,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which planet is the largest planet in our solar system?','Which planet is the largest planet in our solar system?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\", \"Neptune\", \"Uranus\"]','Jupiter','Jupiter is a giant gas planet with mass more than double all other planets combined.','Jupiter is a giant gas planet with mass more than double all other planets combined.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1200,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What stage in the water cycle forms clouds in the sky?','What stage in the water cycle forms clouds in the sky?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Condensation of rising water vapor into droplets\", \"Evaporation of sea water\", \"Precipitation of rain\", \"Transpiration from trees\"]','Condensation of rising water vapor into droplets','Warm water vapor rises, cools at high altitudes, and condenses around dust particles into visible clouds.','Warm water vapor rises, cools at high altitudes, and condenses around dust particles into visible clouds.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1201,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Rain, snow, sleet, and hail falling from clouds to Earth are forms of:','Rain, snow, sleet, and hail falling from clouds to Earth are forms of:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Precipitation\", \"Evaporation\", \"Condensation\", \"Percolation\"]','Precipitation','Precipitation refers to any liquid or frozen moisture that falls from clouds to the ground.','Precipitation refers to any liquid or frozen moisture that falls from clouds to the ground.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1202,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Why does sea water taste salty while rainwater is fresh?','Why does sea water taste salty while rainwater is fresh?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Salts remain behind when sea water evaporates\", \"Rain dissolves salt from clouds\", \"The Sun burns the salt away\", \"Rainwater comes from outer space\"]','Salts remain behind when sea water evaporates','Only pure H₂O molecules evaporate from the ocean surface; heavy dissolved salts remain in the sea.','Only pure H₂O molecules evaporate from the ocean surface; heavy dissolved salts remain in the sea.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1203,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is the process where a solid turns directly into a gas without melting into liquid?','What is the process where a solid turns directly into a gas without melting into liquid?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Sublimation (e.g. Dry ice, mothballs)\", \"Evaporation\", \"Condensation\", \"Freezing\"]','Sublimation (e.g. Dry ice, mothballs)','Sublimation bypasses the liquid state (e.g. solid carbon dioxide dry ice turning into gas).','Sublimation bypasses the liquid state (e.g. solid carbon dioxide dry ice turning into gas).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1204,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which planet is known as the \'Red Planet\' due to iron oxide rust on its surface?','Which planet is known as the \'Red Planet\' due to iron oxide rust on its surface?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mars\", \"Venus\", \"Mercury\", \"Jupiter\"]','Mars','Mars is called the Red Planet because iron-rich dust rusts in its thin atmosphere.','Mars is called the Red Planet because iron-rich dust rusts in its thin atmosphere.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1205,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','How long does the Moon take to complete one orbit around the Earth?','How long does the Moon take to complete one orbit around the Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Approximately 28 to 29.5 days (1 lunar month)\", \"24 hours\", \"365 days\", \"7 days\"]','Approximately 28 to 29.5 days (1 lunar month)','The Moon orbits Earth and completes its phase cycle in roughly 29.5 days.','The Moon orbits Earth and completes its phase cycle in roughly 29.5 days.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1206,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What causes ocean tides on Earth?','What causes ocean tides on Earth?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Gravitational pull of the Moon and Sun on Earth\'s oceans\", \"Earthquakes underwater\", \"Wind blowing across seas\", \"Hot underwater vents\"]','Gravitational pull of the Moon and Sun on Earth\'s oceans','The Moon\'s gravitational attraction pulls water towards it, creating high and low tides.','The Moon\'s gravitational attraction pulls water towards it, creating high and low tides.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1207,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which gas makes up about 78% of the Earth\'s atmosphere?','Which gas makes up about 78% of the Earth\'s atmosphere?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Nitrogen\", \"Oxygen\", \"Carbon dioxide\", \"Hydrogen\"]','Nitrogen','Dry air is composed of roughly 78% Nitrogen, 21% Oxygen, and 1% trace gases.','Dry air is composed of roughly 78% Nitrogen, 21% Oxygen, and 1% trace gases.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1208,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What happens to water particles when water is heated from 20°C to 80°C?','What happens to water particles when water is heated from 20°C to 80°C?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"They gain kinetic energy and move faster and further apart\", \"They slow down and freeze\", \"They disappear\", \"They shrink in mass\"]','They gain kinetic energy and move faster and further apart','Thermal heat increases particle vibration and movement, causing slight expansion.','Thermal heat increases particle vibration and movement, causing slight expansion.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1209,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Why can gases be compressed into smaller containers while solids cannot?','Why can gases be compressed into smaller containers while solids cannot?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Gas particles have large empty spaces between them\", \"Gas particles are softer\", \"Gases have no mass\", \"Solid particles move too fast\"]','Gas particles have large empty spaces between them','Gas molecules are widely spaced, allowing pressure to squeeze them closer together.','Gas molecules are widely spaced, allowing pressure to squeeze them closer together.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1210,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','When dew forms on grass in the early morning, which process has taken place?','When dew forms on grass in the early morning, which process has taken place?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Condensation\", \"Evaporation\", \"Freezing\", \"Transpiration\"]','Condensation','Water vapor in cool night air contacts cold grass blades and condenses into liquid dew droplets.','Water vapor in cool night air contacts cold grass blades and condenses into liquid dew droplets.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1211,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which planet is famous for its bright, prominent system of rings made of ice and rock?','Which planet is famous for its bright, prominent system of rings made of ice and rock?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Saturn\", \"Mars\", \"Venus\", \"Mercury\"]','Saturn','Saturn\'s extensive ring system consists of billions of icy fragments orbiting the planet.','Saturn\'s extensive ring system consists of billions of icy fragments orbiting the planet.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1212,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is the molten rock called while it is still trapped beneath the Earth\'s crust?','What is the molten rock called while it is still trapped beneath the Earth\'s crust?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Magma\", \"Lava\", \"Basalt\", \"Granite\"]','Magma','Beneath Earth\'s surface it is magma; once erupted onto the surface it is called lava.','Beneath Earth\'s surface it is magma; once erupted onto the surface it is called lava.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1213,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Why do we see lightning before we hear the clap of thunder?','Why do we see lightning before we hear the clap of thunder?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Light travels much faster than sound in air\", \"Thunder starts after lightning ends\", \"Sound cannot travel through air\", \"Human eyes are closer than ears\"]','Light travels much faster than sound in air','Light travels at 300,000,000 m/s whereas sound travels at only about 340 m/s in air.','Light travels at 300,000,000 m/s whereas sound travels at only about 340 m/s in air.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1214,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which of the following factors speeds up the evaporation of puddle water?','Which of the following factors speeds up the evaporation of puddle water?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Higher temperature, stronger wind, and larger surface area\", \"High humidity and low wind\", \"Cold weather and shade\", \"Covering the puddle with glass\"]','Higher temperature, stronger wind, and larger surface area','Heat provides energy, wind carries vapor away, and surface area exposes more liquid molecules.','Heat provides energy, wind carries vapor away, and surface area exposes more liquid molecules.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1215,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is an eclipse of the Sun (Solar Eclipse)?','What is an eclipse of the Sun (Solar Eclipse)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The Moon passes directly between the Sun and Earth, casting a shadow on Earth\", \"Earth passes between Sun and Moon\", \"The Sun turns off its light\", \"A comet crashes into the Sun\"]','The Moon passes directly between the Sun and Earth, casting a shadow on Earth','During a solar eclipse, the Moon\'s shadow falls onto parts of the Earth during daytime.','During a solar eclipse, the Moon\'s shadow falls onto parts of the Earth during daytime.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1216,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','What is an eclipse of the Moon (Lunar Eclipse)?','What is an eclipse of the Moon (Lunar Eclipse)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Earth passes directly between Sun and Moon, casting Earth\'s shadow on the Moon\", \"The Moon passes in front of the Sun\", \"The Moon falls into the ocean\", \"Clouds cover the Moon\"]','Earth passes directly between Sun and Moon, casting Earth\'s shadow on the Moon','A lunar eclipse occurs when Earth blocks sunlight from directly illuminating the full Moon.','A lunar eclipse occurs when Earth blocks sunlight from directly illuminating the full Moon.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1217,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which layer of the Earth\'s atmosphere contains the ozone layer that protects us from harmful UV rays?','Which layer of the Earth\'s atmosphere contains the ozone layer that protects us from harmful UV rays?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Stratosphere\", \"Troposphere\", \"Mesosphere\", \"Exosphere\"]','Stratosphere','The ozone layer resides in the stratosphere and absorbs ultraviolet solar radiation.','The ozone layer resides in the stratosphere and absorbs ultraviolet solar radiation.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1218,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Why does ice float on top of liquid water?','Why does ice float on top of liquid water?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Ice is less dense than liquid water\", \"Ice is heavier than water\", \"Ice contains air bubbles only\", \"Ice is a gas\"]','Ice is less dense than liquid water','Water expands upon freezing, giving ice a lower density (~0.92 g/cm³) than liquid water (1.0 g/cm³).','Water expands upon freezing, giving ice a lower density (~0.92 g/cm³) than liquid water (1.0 g/cm³).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1219,'psr_sci_matter_earth','psr_science','Which planet in our solar system is nicknamed the \'Morning Star\' or \'Evening Star\'?','Which planet in our solar system is nicknamed the \'Morning Star\' or \'Evening Star\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Venus\", \"Mars\", \"Jupiter\", \"Saturn\"]','Venus','Venus reflects high sunlight due to thick sulfuric clouds and appears brightly at dawn and dusk.','Venus reflects high sunlight due to thick sulfuric clouds and appears brightly at dawn and dusk.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1220,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Neither the teacher nor the students _______ present at the hall yesterday.','Neither the teacher nor the students _______ present at the hall yesterday.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"were\", \"was\", \"is\", \"are\"]','were','In \'neither... nor\', the verb agrees with the nearer subject (\'students\' is plural -> were).','In \'neither... nor\', the verb agrees with the nearer subject (\'students\' is plural -> were).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1221,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The flock of migratory birds _______ flying south for the winter.','The flock of migratory birds _______ flying south for the winter.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have\"]','is','Collective nouns like \'flock\' take a singular verb when acting as a single unit.','Collective nouns like \'flock\' take a singular verb when acting as a single unit.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1222,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','She _______ her homework before her mother arrived home from work.','She _______ her homework before her mother arrived home from work.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"had finished\", \"has finished\", \"finishes\", \"is finishing\"]','had finished','Past Perfect tense (\'had finished\') indicates an action completed before another past event (\'arrived\').','Past Perfect tense (\'had finished\') indicates an action completed before another past event (\'arrived\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1223,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Neither of the two books _______ available in the national library.','Neither of the two books _______ available in the national library.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have been\"]','is','\'Neither of\' takes a singular verb: \'Neither of the two books is available\'.','\'Neither of\' takes a singular verb: \'Neither of the two books is available\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1224,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','By the time we reach Bandar Seri Begawan tomorrow, the ceremony _______.','By the time we reach Bandar Seri Begawan tomorrow, the ceremony _______.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"will have started\", \"starts\", \"started\", \"has started\"]','will have started','Future Perfect tense (\'will have started\') expresses an action completed before a future time.','Future Perfect tense (\'will have started\') expresses an action completed before a future time.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1225,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Each of the participants _______ given a certificate of achievement.','Each of the participants _______ given a certificate of achievement.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"was\", \"were\", \"are\", \"have\"]','was','\'Each of\' is followed by a singular verb (\'was given\').','\'Each of\' is followed by a singular verb (\'was given\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1226,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Hafiz _______ in Tutong since he was seven years old.','Hafiz _______ in Tutong since he was seven years old.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"has lived\", \"lives\", \"is living\", \"lived\"]','has lived','Present Perfect tense with \'since\' describes an action starting in the past and continuing now.','Present Perfect tense with \'since\' describes an action starting in the past and continuing now.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1227,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','If it _______ heavily tomorrow, the football tournament will be postponed.','If it _______ heavily tomorrow, the football tournament will be postponed.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"rains\", \"will rain\", \"rained\", \"is raining\"]','rains','First conditional: \'If + Simple Present (rains), will + base verb\'.','First conditional: \'If + Simple Present (rains), will + base verb\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1228,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Ten kilometers _______ a long distance to walk in the tropical heat.','Ten kilometers _______ a long distance to walk in the tropical heat.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have been\"]','is','Expressions of distance, money, and time are treated as singular units.','Expressions of distance, money, and time are treated as singular units.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1229,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The doctor advised the patient to _______ sweet drinks to lower blood sugar.','The doctor advised the patient to _______ sweet drinks to lower blood sugar.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"avoid\", \"avoids\", \"avoiding\", \"avoided\"]','avoid','After \'to\' (infinitive), use the base form of the verb: \'to avoid\'.','After \'to\' (infinitive), use the base form of the verb: \'to avoid\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1230,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Ali as well as his cousins _______ invited to the wedding banquet.','Ali as well as his cousins _______ invited to the wedding banquet.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"was\", \"were\", \"are\", \"have been\"]','was','Phrases introduced by \'as well as\' do not change the number of the subject (\'Ali\' is singular -> was).','Phrases introduced by \'as well as\' do not change the number of the subject (\'Ali\' is singular -> was).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1231,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The news broadcast on RTB _______ very encouraging today.','The news broadcast on RTB _______ very encouraging today.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have been\"]','is','\'News\' is an uncountable noun and always takes a singular verb.','\'News\' is an uncountable noun and always takes a singular verb.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1232,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','While we _______ our dinner, the electricity suddenly went out.','While we _______ our dinner, the electricity suddenly went out.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"were having\", \"are having\", \"have had\", \"had had\"]','were having','Past Continuous tense (\'were having\') for an ongoing past action interrupted by another past action (\'went\').','Past Continuous tense (\'were having\') for an ongoing past action interrupted by another past action (\'went\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1233,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Bread and butter _______ his favourite breakfast every morning.','Bread and butter _______ his favourite breakfast every morning.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have been\"]','is','Compound subjects thought of as a single dish/concept take a singular verb.','Compound subjects thought of as a single dish/concept take a singular verb.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1234,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The detective noticed that someone _______ the front door lock.','The detective noticed that someone _______ the front door lock.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"had tampered with\", \"has tampered with\", \"is tampering\", \"tamper\"]','had tampered with','Past Perfect for an action that happened before the detective\'s past observation.','Past Perfect for an action that happened before the detective\'s past observation.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1235,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','They _______ for the bus for over forty minutes before it finally arrived.','They _______ for the bus for over forty minutes before it finally arrived.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"had been waiting\", \"have waited\", \"are waiting\", \"waited\"]','had been waiting','Past Perfect Continuous emphasizes the duration of an activity before another past event.','Past Perfect Continuous emphasizes the duration of an activity before another past event.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1236,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Physics _______ a challenging subject for many secondary school students.','Physics _______ a challenging subject for many secondary school students.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"being\"]','is','Subject names ending in \'s\' (Physics, Mathematics, Civics) take a singular verb.','Subject names ending in \'s\' (Physics, Mathematics, Civics) take a singular verb.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1237,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Everyone in the grand auditorium _______ silent when His Majesty entered.','Everyone in the grand auditorium _______ silent when His Majesty entered.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"was\", \"were\", \"are\", \"have been\"]','was','Indefinite pronouns like \'Everyone\', \'Someone\', \'Nobody\' take singular verbs.','Indefinite pronouns like \'Everyone\', \'Someone\', \'Nobody\' take singular verbs.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1238,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The athlete _______ hard every single day to qualify for the SEA Games.','The athlete _______ hard every single day to qualify for the SEA Games.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"trains\", \"train\", \"training\", \"have trained\"]','trains','Third-person singular present tense requires \'s\': \'The athlete trains\'.','Third-person singular present tense requires \'s\': \'The athlete trains\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1239,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','She speaks French fluently, _______ she?','She speaks French fluently, _______ she?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"doesn\'t\", \"does\", \"isn\'t\", \"wasn\'t\"]','doesn\'t','Positive statement in Simple Present uses negative question tag \'doesn\'t she?\'.','Positive statement in Simple Present uses negative question tag \'doesn\'t she?\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1240,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','None of the spilled milk _______ salvageable.','None of the spilled milk _______ salvageable.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"was\", \"were\", \"are\", \"have been\"]','was','\'Milk\' is uncountable, so \'None of the milk\' takes a singular verb (\'was\').','\'Milk\' is uncountable, so \'None of the milk\' takes a singular verb (\'was\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1241,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','You haven\'t submitted your science project yet, _______ you?','You haven\'t submitted your science project yet, _______ you?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"have\", \"haven\'t\", \"did\", \"didn\'t\"]','have','Negative statement takes a positive question tag (\'haven\'t you? -> have you?\').','Negative statement takes a positive question tag (\'haven\'t you? -> have you?\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1242,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The pair of scissors _______ kept in the top drawer.','The pair of scissors _______ kept in the top drawer.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"have been\"]','is','\'The pair\' is singular, so it takes a singular verb (\'is kept\').','\'The pair\' is singular, so it takes a singular verb (\'is kept\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1243,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','I wish I _______ more time to complete the English composition paper.','I wish I _______ more time to complete the English composition paper.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"had\", \"have\", \"having\", \"am having\"]','had','Hypothetical wish in the present uses the subjunctive past form (\'had\').','Hypothetical wish in the present uses the subjunctive past form (\'had\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1244,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','The principal insisted that every student _______ the school uniform.','The principal insisted that every student _______ the school uniform.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"wear\", \"wears\", \"wore\", \"wearing\"]','wear','Subjunctive mood after \'insisted that\' uses base verb (\'wear\').','Subjunctive mood after \'insisted that\' uses base verb (\'wear\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1245,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Neither car _______ damaged in the minor collision.','Neither car _______ damaged in the minor collision.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"was\", \"were\", \"are\", \"have been\"]','was','\'Neither\' followed by a singular noun takes a singular verb (\'was\').','\'Neither\' followed by a singular noun takes a singular verb (\'was\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1246,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Look at those dark clouds! It _______ rain soon.','Look at those dark clouds! It _______ rain soon.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is going to\", \"will have\", \"rained\", \"was raining\"]','is going to','\'Going to\' is used for future predictions supported by present visual evidence.','\'Going to\' is used for future predictions supported by present visual evidence.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1247,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Three hundred dollars _______ too much to pay for a simple pair of shoes.','Three hundred dollars _______ too much to pay for a simple pair of shoes.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"is\", \"are\", \"were\", \"being\"]','is','Sums of money take singular verbs.','Sums of money take singular verbs.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1248,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','Hardly had the bell rung when the pupils _______ out of the classroom.','Hardly had the bell rung when the pupils _______ out of the classroom.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"rushed\", \"rush\", \"rushing\", \"have rushed\"]','rushed','\'Hardly had... when\' connects past perfect with simple past (\'rushed\').','\'Hardly had... when\' connects past perfect with simple past (\'rushed\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1249,'psr_eng_grammar_tenses','psr_english','He _______ to school on foot every day because his house is nearby.','He _______ to school on foot every day because his house is nearby.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"walks\", \"walk\", \"walking\", \"has walked\"]','walks','Habitual regular action takes Simple Present: \'He walks\'.','Habitual regular action takes Simple Present: \'He walks\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1250,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The adventurous boys jumped _______ the river to cool off on a hot afternoon.','The adventurous boys jumped _______ the river to cool off on a hot afternoon.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"into\", \"onto\", \"in\", \"to\"]','into','\'Into\' indicates movement from outside to inside a body of water.','\'Into\' indicates movement from outside to inside a body of water.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1251,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The Independence Day celebration will commence _______ 8:00 a.m. sharp.','The Independence Day celebration will commence _______ 8:00 a.m. sharp.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"at\", \"on\", \"in\", \"by\"]','at','Use \'at\' for specific clock times (\'at 8:00 a.m.\').','Use \'at\' for specific clock times (\'at 8:00 a.m.\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1252,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','Brunei National Day is proudly celebrated _______ the 23rd of February every year.','Brunei National Day is proudly celebrated _______ the 23rd of February every year.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"on\", \"in\", \"at\", \"during\"]','on','Use \'on\' for specific calendar dates and days (\'on the 23rd of February\').','Use \'on\' for specific calendar dates and days (\'on the 23rd of February\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1253,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The girl _______ won the national public speaking competition is my classmate.','The girl _______ won the national public speaking competition is my classmate.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"who\", \"whom\", \"which\", \"whose\"]','who','\'Who\' is the subject relative pronoun referring to people (\'The girl who won\').','\'Who\' is the subject relative pronoun referring to people (\'The girl who won\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1254,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The historic book _______ cover was torn has been carefully repaired by the librarian.','The historic book _______ cover was torn has been carefully repaired by the librarian.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"whose\", \"which\", \"whom\", \"who\"]','whose','\'Whose\' shows possession for both people and things (\'whose cover\').','\'Whose\' shows possession for both people and things (\'whose cover\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1255,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','He worked diligently day and night _______ he could secure a scholarship.','He worked diligently day and night _______ he could secure a scholarship.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"so that\", \"although\", \"unless\", \"whereas\"]','so that','\'So that\' expresses purpose or intention.','\'So that\' expresses purpose or intention.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1256,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','_______ she felt exhausted after the long hike, she continued walking up the hill.','_______ she felt exhausted after the long hike, she continued walking up the hill.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Although\", \"Because\", \"Since\", \"Unless\"]','Although','\'Although\' introduces a clause of contrast or concession.','\'Although\' introduces a clause of contrast or concession.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1257,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','You will not pass the examination _______ you revise your notes consistently.','You will not pass the examination _______ you revise your notes consistently.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"unless\", \"if\", \"because\", \"so\"]','unless','\'Unless\' means \'if not\': \'Unless you revise, you will not pass\'.','\'Unless\' means \'if not\': \'Unless you revise, you will not pass\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1258,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The kitten hid _______ the sofa because it was frightened by the thunder.','The kitten hid _______ the sofa because it was frightened by the thunder.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"under\", \"between\", \"among\", \"over\"]','under','\'Under\' denotes position beneath a physical object.','\'Under\' denotes position beneath a physical object.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1259,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','Distribute the sweets equally _______ the four children.','Distribute the sweets equally _______ the four children.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"among\", \"between\", \"with\", \"to\"]','among','Use \'between\' for two items/people, and \'among\' for three or more.','Use \'between\' for two items/people, and \'among\' for three or more.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1260,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The bridge was constructed _______ the Tutong River to connect two villages.','The bridge was constructed _______ the Tutong River to connect two villages.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"across\", \"through\", \"along\", \"over\"]','across','\'Across\' signifies spanning from one side of a river/road to the other.','\'Across\' signifies spanning from one side of a river/road to the other.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1261,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','He walked _______ the dense jungle path until he spotted the waterfall.','He walked _______ the dense jungle path until he spotted the waterfall.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"along\", \"across\", \"between\", \"over\"]','along','\'Along\' indicates movement parallel to the direction of a path or road.','\'Along\' indicates movement parallel to the direction of a path or road.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1262,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','To _______ did you lend your English dictionary?','To _______ did you lend your English dictionary?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"whom\", \"who\", \"which\", \"whose\"]','whom','\'Whom\' is the objective pronoun used after prepositions (\'To whom\').','\'Whom\' is the objective pronoun used after prepositions (\'To whom\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1263,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The boy made the wooden toy all by _______.','The boy made the wooden toy all by _______.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"himself\", \"itself\", \"herself\", \"themselves\"]','himself','Reflexive pronoun for a male singular subject (\'The boy -> himself\').','Reflexive pronoun for a male singular subject (\'The boy -> himself\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1264,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','She poured the hot tea _______ the porcelain cup.','She poured the hot tea _______ the porcelain cup.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"into\", \"onto\", \"at\", \"in\"]','into','Movement into an enclosure requires \'into\'.','Movement into an enclosure requires \'into\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1265,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The plane flew high _______ the storm clouds.','The plane flew high _______ the storm clouds.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"above\", \"on\", \"at\", \"into\"]','above','\'Above\' indicates a higher vertical altitude without physical contact.','\'Above\' indicates a higher vertical altitude without physical contact.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1266,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','Neither Kamal _______ Danial attended the extra tuition class.','Neither Kamal _______ Danial attended the extra tuition class.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"nor\", \"or\", \"and\", \"but\"]','nor','The correlative conjunction pair is \'neither... nor\' (and \'either... or\').','The correlative conjunction pair is \'neither... nor\' (and \'either... or\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1267,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','I have not seen my primary school teacher _______ last December.','I have not seen my primary school teacher _______ last December.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"since\", \"for\", \"during\", \"at\"]','since','Use \'since\' with a specific starting point in time (\'since last December\').','Use \'since\' with a specific starting point in time (\'since last December\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1268,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','They stayed at the beach resort _______ three consecutive days.','They stayed at the beach resort _______ three consecutive days.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"for\", \"since\", \"during\", \"while\"]','for','Use \'for\' with a duration of time (\'for three days\').','Use \'for\' with a duration of time (\'for three days\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1269,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','Despite _______ unwell, the brave young soldier reported for duty.','Despite _______ unwell, the brave young soldier reported for duty.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"feeling\", \"felt\", \"feels\", \"feel\"]','feeling','Prepositions and prepositions phrases like \'Despite\' take a gerund (-ing form).','Prepositions and prepositions phrases like \'Despite\' take a gerund (-ing form).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1270,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The car stopped _______ the traffic light because it turned red.','The car stopped _______ the traffic light because it turned red.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"at\", \"on\", \"in\", \"to\"]','at','Use \'at\' for designated traffic points (\'at the traffic light\').','Use \'at\' for designated traffic points (\'at the traffic light\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1271,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The passengers walked _______ the narrow tunnel to board the aircraft.','The passengers walked _______ the narrow tunnel to board the aircraft.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"through\", \"across\", \"between\", \"over\"]','through','\'Through\' denotes movement inside a three-dimensional enclosed space.','\'Through\' denotes movement inside a three-dimensional enclosed space.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1272,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','He is not only intelligent _______ very humble and helpful.','He is not only intelligent _______ very humble and helpful.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"but also\", \"and also\", \"as well as\", \"together with\"]','but also','Correlative conjunction pair: \'not only... but also\'.','Correlative conjunction pair: \'not only... but also\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1273,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','My father parked his car _______ the two tall palm trees.','My father parked his car _______ the two tall palm trees.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"between\", \"among\", \"in\", \"at\"]','between','Use \'between\' when referring to exactly two reference points.','Use \'between\' when referring to exactly two reference points.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1274,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','She was rewarded _______ her honesty and integrity.','She was rewarded _______ her honesty and integrity.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"for\", \"with\", \"by\", \"from\"]','for','One is rewarded \'for\' a virtuous quality or deed.','One is rewarded \'for\' a virtuous quality or deed.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1275,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The students listened _______ to the safety briefing before the science experiment.','The students listened _______ to the safety briefing before the science experiment.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"attentively\", \"attentive\", \"attention\", \"attentiveness\"]','attentively','An adverb of manner (\'attentively\') describes how the verb \'listened\' was done.','An adverb of manner (\'attentively\') describes how the verb \'listened\' was done.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1276,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','This antique pocket watch belonged to my grandfather; it is _______.','This antique pocket watch belonged to my grandfather; it is _______.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"mine\", \"my\", \"me\", \"myself\"]','mine','Possessive pronoun standing alone without a following noun is \'mine\'.','Possessive pronoun standing alone without a following noun is \'mine\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1277,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The dog barked fiercely _______ the stranger approaching the gate.','The dog barked fiercely _______ the stranger approaching the gate.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"at\", \"on\", \"to\", \"with\"]','at','The standard preposition after \'bark\' is \'at\'.','The standard preposition after \'bark\' is \'at\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1278,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','We must leave immediately, _______ we will miss the morning ferry to Temburong.','We must leave immediately, _______ we will miss the morning ferry to Temburong.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"otherwise\", \"whereas\", \"although\", \"since\"]','otherwise','\'Otherwise\' means \'or else\' to indicate an adverse consequence.','\'Otherwise\' means \'or else\' to indicate an adverse consequence.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1279,'psr_eng_parts_of_speech','psr_english','The athlete was disqualified _______ breaking the starting lane rules.','The athlete was disqualified _______ breaking the starting lane rules.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"for\", \"because\", \"so\", \"with\"]','for','\'Disqualified for\' followed by gerund expresses the reason for penalty.','\'Disqualified for\' followed by gerund expresses the reason for penalty.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1280,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the idiom \'a piece of cake\' mean?','What does the idiom \'a piece of cake\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Very easy to accomplish\", \"A sweet dessert\", \"Very expensive\", \"Difficult to understand\"]','Very easy to accomplish','\'A piece of cake\' is an English idiom meaning something extremely simple or effortless.','\'A piece of cake\' is an English idiom meaning something extremely simple or effortless.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1281,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','When someone says they are \'feeling under the weather\', they mean they are:','When someone says they are \'feeling under the weather\', they mean they are:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Feeling slightly ill or sick\", \"Experiencing cold rain\", \"Very joyful\", \"Angry at the weather\"]','Feeling slightly ill or sick','\'Under the weather\' means unwell or unwell in health.','\'Under the weather\' means unwell or unwell in health.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1282,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What is the meaning of the phrasal verb \'give up\'?','What is the meaning of the phrasal verb \'give up\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Stop trying or surrender\", \"Donate money\", \"Offer a present\", \"Rise early\"]','Stop trying or surrender','\'Give up\' means to cease an effort or abandon hope.','\'Give up\' means to cease an effort or abandon hope.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1283,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the word that is opposite in meaning (antonym) to \'GENEROUS\':','Choose the word that is opposite in meaning (antonym) to \'GENEROUS\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Stingy\", \"Kind\", \"Courteous\", \"Polite\"]','Stingy','\'Generous\' means willing to give freely; its antonym is \'stingy\' or \'miserly\'.','\'Generous\' means willing to give freely; its antonym is \'stingy\' or \'miserly\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1284,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the word closest in meaning (synonym) to \'HAZARDOUS\':','Choose the word closest in meaning (synonym) to \'HAZARDOUS\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Dangerous\", \"Safe\", \"Secure\", \"Gentle\"]','Dangerous','\'Hazardous\' describes something perilous or dangerous.','\'Hazardous\' describes something perilous or dangerous.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1285,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does it mean to \'burn the midnight oil\'?','What does it mean to \'burn the midnight oil\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Study or work late into the night\", \"Waste lamp kerosene\", \"Cause a kitchen fire\", \"Wake up before sunrise\"]','Study or work late into the night','\'Burn the midnight oil\' means working diligently late past bedtime.','\'Burn the midnight oil\' means working diligently late past bedtime.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1286,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','The firefighter was commended for his \'valour\'. What does \'valour\' mean?','The firefighter was commended for his \'valour\'. What does \'valour\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Great bravery and courage\", \"Physical strength\", \"Speed and agility\", \"Cleverness\"]','Great bravery and courage','\'Valour\' means heroic courage in the face of danger.','\'Valour\' means heroic courage in the face of danger.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1287,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the idiom \'once in a blue moon\' mean?','What does the idiom \'once in a blue moon\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Very rarely\", \"Every month\", \"During nighttime\", \"Frequently\"]','Very rarely','\'Once in a blue moon\' signifies an occurrence that happens extremely seldom.','\'Once in a blue moon\' signifies an occurrence that happens extremely seldom.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1288,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the phrasal verb \'call off\' mean in \'They had to call off the match\'?','What does the phrasal verb \'call off\' mean in \'They had to call off the match\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Cancel\", \"Postpone\", \"Continue\", \"Start\"]','Cancel','\'Call off\' means to cancel an event entirely.','\'Call off\' means to cancel an event entirely.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1289,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the correct spelling:','Choose the correct spelling:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Accommodation\", \"Acommodation\", \"Accomodation\", \"Acomodation\"]','Accommodation','Accommodation is spelled with double \'c\' and double \'m\'.','Accommodation is spelled with double \'c\' and double \'m\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1290,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the idiom \'spill the beans\' mean?','What does the idiom \'spill the beans\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Reveal a secret prematurely\", \"Drop groceries\", \"Cook dinner\", \"Tell the truth in court\"]','Reveal a secret prematurely','\'Spill the beans\' means to disclose confidential information.','\'Spill the beans\' means to disclose confidential information.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1291,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the synonym for \'ABUNDANT\':','Choose the synonym for \'ABUNDANT\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Plentiful\", \"Scarce\", \"Sparse\", \"Tiny\"]','Plentiful','\'Abundant\' means existing in large quantities or plentiful.','\'Abundant\' means existing in large quantities or plentiful.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1292,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does \'break the ice\' mean in a social gathering?','What does \'break the ice\' mean in a social gathering?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Overcome initial shyness and start conversation\", \"Drop an ice cube\", \"Chill a drink\", \"End an argument\"]','Overcome initial shyness and start conversation','\'Break the ice\' means initiating friendly conversation in an awkward or formal setting.','\'Break the ice\' means initiating friendly conversation in an awkward or formal setting.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1293,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the antonym for \'ANCIENT\':','Choose the antonym for \'ANCIENT\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Modern\", \"Antique\", \"Old\", \"Historic\"]','Modern','\'Ancient\' refers to long ago; its direct opposite is \'modern\'.','\'Ancient\' refers to long ago; its direct opposite is \'modern\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1294,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the phrasal verb \'look up to\' mean in \'Young players look up to the captain\'?','What does the phrasal verb \'look up to\' mean in \'Young players look up to the captain\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Admire and respect\", \"Look at the ceiling\", \"Search in a book\", \"Supervise\"]','Admire and respect','\'Look up to someone\' means to regard them with deep admiration and respect.','\'Look up to someone\' means to regard them with deep admiration and respect.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1295,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','The weather was \'unpredictable\'. What does \'unpredictable\' mean?','The weather was \'unpredictable\'. What does \'unpredictable\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Likely to change unexpectedly\", \"Very hot\", \"Calm and peaceful\", \"Predictable\"]','Likely to change unexpectedly','Prefix \'un-\' means not; unpredictable means cannot be foreseen with certainty.','Prefix \'un-\' means not; unpredictable means cannot be foreseen with certainty.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1296,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What is the meaning of the idiom \'cost an arm and a leg\'?','What is the meaning of the idiom \'cost an arm and a leg\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Extremely expensive\", \"Very cheap\", \"Painful to carry\", \"Worth nothing\"]','Extremely expensive','If an item costs an arm and a leg, it is excessively pricey.','If an item costs an arm and a leg, it is excessively pricey.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1297,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the synonym for \'COMMENCE\':','Choose the synonym for \'COMMENCE\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Begin\", \"Finish\", \"Pause\", \"Delay\"]','Begin','\'Commence\' is a formal verb meaning to begin or start.','\'Commence\' is a formal verb meaning to begin or start.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1298,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does it mean to \'turn a deaf ear\' to advice?','What does it mean to \'turn a deaf ear\' to advice?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Refuse to listen or ignore\", \"Have hearing trouble\", \"Clean one\'s ear\", \"Agree wholeheartedly\"]','Refuse to listen or ignore','\'Turn a deaf ear\' means willfully ignoring someone\'s warning or advice.','\'Turn a deaf ear\' means willfully ignoring someone\'s warning or advice.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1299,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the antonym for \'ARROGANT\':','Choose the antonym for \'ARROGANT\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Humble\", \"Proud\", \"Boastful\", \"Haughty\"]','Humble','\'Arrogant\' means having an exaggerated sense of self-importance; opposite is \'humble\'.','\'Arrogant\' means having an exaggerated sense of self-importance; opposite is \'humble\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1300,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the phrasal verb \'put off\' mean in \'Never put off till tomorrow what you can do today\'?','What does the phrasal verb \'put off\' mean in \'Never put off till tomorrow what you can do today\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Postpone or delay\", \"Extinguish\", \"Wear clothes\", \"Discard\"]','Postpone or delay','\'Put off\' means to delay doing something until a later time.','\'Put off\' means to delay doing something until a later time.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1301,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','The word \'fragile\' on a parcel warns handlers that the contents are:','The word \'fragile\' on a parcel warns handlers that the contents are:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Easily broken or damaged\", \"Very heavy\", \"Flammable\", \"Waterproof\"]','Easily broken or damaged','\'Fragile\' items (like glass and porcelain) crack or break easily if dropped.','\'Fragile\' items (like glass and porcelain) crack or break easily if dropped.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1302,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the idiom \'see eye to eye\' mean?','What does the idiom \'see eye to eye\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Agree completely with someone\", \"Stare angrily\", \"Wear glasses\", \"Meet in person\"]','Agree completely with someone','\'See eye to eye\' means to have identical opinions and agree.','\'See eye to eye\' means to have identical opinions and agree.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1303,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the correct word: \'The judge was known for his _______ judgment.\'','Choose the correct word: \'The judge was known for his _______ judgment.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"impartial\", \"partial\", \"biased\", \"prejudiced\"]','impartial','\'Impartial\' means fair, unbiased, and treating all parties equally.','\'Impartial\' means fair, unbiased, and treating all parties equally.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1304,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does \'hit the nail on the head\' mean?','What does \'hit the nail on the head\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"State an exact truth accurately\", \"Use a hammer properly\", \"Injure a finger\", \"Make a loud noise\"]','State an exact truth accurately','\'Hit the nail on the head\' means describing the precise cause or truth of a situation.','\'Hit the nail on the head\' means describing the precise cause or truth of a situation.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1305,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the synonym for \'SWIFT\':','Choose the synonym for \'SWIFT\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Rapid\", \"Sluggish\", \"Heavy\", \"Careless\"]','Rapid','\'Swift\' means moving with great speed or rapid.','\'Swift\' means moving with great speed or rapid.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1306,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the phrasal verb \'run out of\' mean in \'We have run out of printer paper\'?','What does the phrasal verb \'run out of\' mean in \'We have run out of printer paper\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Exhaust the supply of something\", \"Sprint outdoors\", \"Throw away\", \"Buy extra\"]','Exhaust the supply of something','\'Run out of\' means having depleted the available stock of a resource.','\'Run out of\' means having depleted the available stock of a resource.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1307,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','Choose the antonym for \'OBEDIENT\':','Choose the antonym for \'OBEDIENT\':','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Rebellious\", \"Compliant\", \"Dutiful\", \"Respectful\"]','Rebellious','\'Obedient\' means following instructions; its opposite is \'rebellious\' or \'defiant\'.','\'Obedient\' means following instructions; its opposite is \'rebellious\' or \'defiant\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1308,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What is an \'amphibian\'?','What is an \'amphibian\'?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"An animal able to live both on land and in water\", \"A creature that flies\", \"A plant with spores\", \"A deep-sea fish\"]','An animal able to live both on land and in water','Amphibians (like frogs and salamanders) live in water and on land during their life cycles.','Amphibians (like frogs and salamanders) live in water and on land during their life cycles.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1309,'psr_eng_vocabulary_idioms','psr_english','What does the idiom \'barking up the wrong tree\' mean?','What does the idiom \'barking up the wrong tree\' mean?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Pursuing a mistaken line of thought or action\", \"Scolding a pet\", \"Climbing trees\", \"Losing a track\"]','Pursuing a mistaken line of thought or action','\'Barking up the wrong tree\' means blaming the wrong person or following a false assumption.','\'Barking up the wrong tree\' means blaming the wrong person or following a false assumption.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1310,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'The mechanic repaired the damaged car.\'','Change to passive voice: \'The mechanic repaired the damaged car.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The damaged car was repaired by the mechanic.\", \"The damaged car is repaired by the mechanic.\", \"The mechanic was repaired by the car.\", \"The damaged car had been repaired.\"]','The damaged car was repaired by the mechanic.','Simple past active (\'repaired\') becomes past passive (\'was repaired by\').','Simple past active (\'repaired\') becomes past passive (\'was repaired by\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1311,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'The chef is preparing a delicious dessert.\'','Change to passive voice: \'The chef is preparing a delicious dessert.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"A delicious dessert is being prepared by the chef.\", \"A delicious dessert was prepared by the chef.\", \"A delicious dessert is prepared by the chef.\", \"A delicious dessert has been prepared.\"]','A delicious dessert is being prepared by the chef.','Present continuous active (\'is preparing\') becomes \'is being prepared\'.','Present continuous active (\'is preparing\') becomes \'is being prepared\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1312,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to indirect speech: \'I am reading an adventure novel,\' said Danial.','Convert to indirect speech: \'I am reading an adventure novel,\' said Danial.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Danial said that he was reading an adventure novel.\", \"Danial said that he is reading an adventure novel.\", \"Danial said that I was reading an adventure novel.\", \"Danial says that he was reading an adventure novel.\"]','Danial said that he was reading an adventure novel.','Direct \'I am reading\' shifts back in tense to \'he was reading\' in reported speech.','Direct \'I am reading\' shifts back in tense to \'he was reading\' in reported speech.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1313,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to indirect speech: \'Where do you live?\' asked the police officer.','Convert to indirect speech: \'Where do you live?\' asked the police officer.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The police officer asked where I lived.\", \"The police officer asked where did I live.\", \"The police officer asked where do I live.\", \"The police officer asked where I had lived.\"]','The police officer asked where I lived.','In reported questions, do-support drops and word order becomes subject + verb: \'where I lived\'.','In reported questions, do-support drops and word order becomes subject + verb: \'where I lived\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1314,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'Although\': \'It was raining heavily. The boys continued playing football.\'','Combine using \'Although\': \'It was raining heavily. The boys continued playing football.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Although it was raining heavily, the boys continued playing football.\", \"Although the boys played football, it rained heavily.\", \"It was raining heavily although the boys continued.\", \"The boys continued although raining heavily.\"]','Although it was raining heavily, the boys continued playing football.','\'Although\' shows concession at the beginning of the dependent contrast clause.','\'Although\' shows concession at the beginning of the dependent contrast clause.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1315,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to active voice: \'The national anthem was sung by the school choir.\'','Change to active voice: \'The national anthem was sung by the school choir.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The school choir sang the national anthem.\", \"The school choir was singing the anthem.\", \"The school choir sings the anthem.\", \"The school choir has sung the anthem.\"]','The school choir sang the national anthem.','Passive \'was sung by the choir\' converts into simple past active \'The school choir sang\'.','Passive \'was sung by the choir\' converts into simple past active \'The school choir sang\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1316,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Choose the correct punctuation: \'Where did you put my glasses _______\'','Choose the correct punctuation: \'Where did you put my glasses _______\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"?\", \".\", \"!\", \",\"]','?','Direct questions must end with a question mark (?).','Direct questions must end with a question mark (?).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1317,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to indirect speech: \'Do not play near the busy road,\' mother told the children.','Convert to indirect speech: \'Do not play near the busy road,\' mother told the children.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Mother warned the children not to play near the busy road.\", \"Mother told the children do not play near the road.\", \"Mother said the children to not play near the road.\", \"Mother asked the children not playing near the road.\"]','Mother warned the children not to play near the busy road.','Imperative commands convert to \'told/warned + object + not to + base verb\'.','Imperative commands convert to \'told/warned + object + not to + base verb\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1318,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'Both... and\': \'Siti likes reading. Aini likes reading.\'','Combine using \'Both... and\': \'Siti likes reading. Aini likes reading.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Both Siti and Aini like reading.\", \"Both Siti and Aini likes reading.\", \"Both Siti with Aini like reading.\", \"Siti and Aini both likes reading.\"]','Both Siti and Aini like reading.','Correlative \'Both... and\' forms a plural subject and takes plural verb \'like\'.','Correlative \'Both... and\' forms a plural subject and takes plural verb \'like\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1319,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'The earthquake destroyed hundreds of buildings.\'','Change to passive voice: \'The earthquake destroyed hundreds of buildings.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Hundreds of buildings were destroyed by the earthquake.\", \"Hundreds of buildings was destroyed by the earthquake.\", \"Hundreds of buildings are destroyed by the earthquake.\", \"The earthquake was destroyed by buildings.\"]','Hundreds of buildings were destroyed by the earthquake.','\'Hundreds of buildings\' is plural, so use \'were destroyed\'.','\'Hundreds of buildings\' is plural, so use \'were destroyed\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1320,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Identify the sentence with correct capitalization:','Identify the sentence with correct capitalization:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"His Majesty Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah visited the district of Temburong.\", \"his majesty sultan haji hassanal bolkiah visited temburong.\", \"His majesty Sultan haji hassanal bolkiah Visited Temburong.\", \"His Majesty sultan Haji hassanal Bolkiah visited temburong.\"]','His Majesty Sultan Haji Hassanal Bolkiah visited the district of Temburong.','Royal titles, personal names, and geographical districts must be capitalized.','Royal titles, personal names, and geographical districts must be capitalized.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1321,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'Neither... nor\': \'He does not drink tea. He does not drink coffee.\'','Combine using \'Neither... nor\': \'He does not drink tea. He does not drink coffee.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"He drinks neither tea nor coffee.\", \"He drinks neither tea or coffee.\", \"Neither he drinks tea nor coffee.\", \"He does not drink neither tea nor coffee.\"]','He drinks neither tea nor coffee.','\'Neither... nor\' replaces negative words without double negation: \'drinks neither tea nor coffee\'.','\'Neither... nor\' replaces negative words without double negation: \'drinks neither tea nor coffee\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1322,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to indirect speech: \'I will submit the assignment tomorrow,\' promised Farid.','Convert to indirect speech: \'I will submit the assignment tomorrow,\' promised Farid.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Farid promised that he would submit the assignment the next day.\", \"Farid promised that he will submit the assignment tomorrow.\", \"Farid promised that I would submit the assignment.\", \"Farid promised that he would submit the assignment tomorrow.\"]','Farid promised that he would submit the assignment the next day.','\'Will\' shifts to \'would\', and \'tomorrow\' shifts to \'the next day\' in reported speech.','\'Will\' shifts to \'would\', and \'tomorrow\' shifts to \'the next day\' in reported speech.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1323,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'Someone has stolen my bicycle.\'','Change to passive voice: \'Someone has stolen my bicycle.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"My bicycle has been stolen.\", \"My bicycle was stolen by someone.\", \"My bicycle is been stolen.\", \"Someone was stolen my bicycle.\"]','My bicycle has been stolen.','Present perfect passive: \'has stolen\' -> \'has been stolen\'.','Present perfect passive: \'has stolen\' -> \'has been stolen\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1324,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Choose the correct relative clause: \'The laptop _______ I bought yesterday is very fast.\'','Choose the correct relative clause: \'The laptop _______ I bought yesterday is very fast.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"which\", \"who\", \"whose\", \"whom\"]','which','Inanimate objects take \'which\' or \'that\'.','Inanimate objects take \'which\' or \'that\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1325,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'so... that\': \'The luggage was very heavy. She could not lift it.\'','Combine using \'so... that\': \'The luggage was very heavy. She could not lift it.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The luggage was so heavy that she could not lift it.\", \"The luggage was heavy so that she could not lift it.\", \"Because the luggage was so heavy that she lifted it.\", \"The luggage was very heavy that she could not lift it.\"]','The luggage was so heavy that she could not lift it.','Structure: \'so + adjective + that + result clause\'.','Structure: \'so + adjective + that + result clause\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1326,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to active voice: \'The novel was written by a famous Bruneian author.\'','Change to active voice: \'The novel was written by a famous Bruneian author.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"A famous Bruneian author wrote the novel.\", \"A famous Bruneian author was writing the novel.\", \"A famous Bruneian author writes the novel.\", \"The novel wrote a famous Bruneian author.\"]','A famous Bruneian author wrote the novel.','The agent \'A famous Bruneian author\' becomes the subject in simple past active.','The agent \'A famous Bruneian author\' becomes the subject in simple past active.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1327,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Choose the sentence with correct apostrophe usage for possession:','Choose the sentence with correct apostrophe usage for possession:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The girls\' bicycles were parked neatly in the shed.\", \"The girl\'s bicycles were parked neatly in the shed.\", \"The girls bicycles\' were parked neatly in the shed.\", \"The girls bicycle\'s were parked neatly in the shed.\"]','The girls\' bicycles were parked neatly in the shed.','For plural nouns ending in \'s\', add the apostrophe after the \'s\' (girls\').','For plural nouns ending in \'s\', add the apostrophe after the \'s\' (girls\').','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1328,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to reported speech: \'Can you swim across the river?\' he asked me.','Convert to reported speech: \'Can you swim across the river?\' he asked me.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"He asked me if I could swim across the river.\", \"He asked me that can I swim across the river.\", \"He asked me if I can swim across the river.\", \"He asked me could I swim across the river.\"]','He asked me if I could swim across the river.','Yes/No questions use \'if/whether\' + subject + past modal \'could\'.','Yes/No questions use \'if/whether\' + subject + past modal \'could\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1329,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'in order to\': \'He exercised every morning. He wanted to maintain his fitness.\'','Combine using \'in order to\': \'He exercised every morning. He wanted to maintain his fitness.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"He exercised every morning in order to maintain his fitness.\", \"In order to exercise every morning he wanted fitness.\", \"He wanted fitness in order to he exercised.\", \"He exercised so in order to maintain fitness.\"]','He exercised every morning in order to maintain his fitness.','\'In order to + base verb\' concisely connects action to objective.','\'In order to + base verb\' concisely connects action to objective.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1330,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Choose the correct tag: \'Let\'s visit the Brunei Arts and Handicraft Centre, _______?\'','Choose the correct tag: \'Let\'s visit the Brunei Arts and Handicraft Centre, _______?\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"shall we\", \"will you\", \"don\'t we\", \"aren\'t we\"]','shall we','Suggestions starting with \'Let\'s\' always take the question tag \'shall we?\'.','Suggestions starting with \'Let\'s\' always take the question tag \'shall we?\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1331,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'They will announce the PSR examination results next week.\'','Change to passive voice: \'They will announce the PSR examination results next week.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The PSR examination results will be announced next week.\", \"The PSR examination results are announced next week.\", \"The PSR examination results will announce next week.\", \"The PSR examination results have been announced.\"]','The PSR examination results will be announced next week.','Future simple passive: \'will + be + past participle (announced)\'.','Future simple passive: \'will + be + past participle (announced)\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1332,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Identify the compound sentence:','Identify the compound sentence:','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The bell rang, and the children cheered enthusiastically.\", \"Because the bell rang, the children cheered.\", \"The children cheered loudly after hearing the bell.\", \"Hearing the bell, the children cheered.\"]','The bell rang, and the children cheered enthusiastically.','A compound sentence contains two independent clauses joined by coordinating conjunction \'and\'.','A compound sentence contains two independent clauses joined by coordinating conjunction \'and\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1333,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to indirect speech: \'I must complete my chores now,\' said Sara.','Convert to indirect speech: \'I must complete my chores now,\' said Sara.','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Sara said that she had to complete her chores then.\", \"Sara said that she must complete her chores now.\", \"Sara said that she has to complete her chores then.\", \"Sara said that she had to complete her chores now.\"]','Sara said that she had to complete her chores then.','\'Must\' shifts to \'had to\', and \'now\' shifts to \'then\'.','\'Must\' shifts to \'had to\', and \'now\' shifts to \'then\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1334,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'too... to\': \'The coffee is very hot. I cannot drink it.\'','Combine using \'too... to\': \'The coffee is very hot. I cannot drink it.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The coffee is too hot for me to drink.\", \"The coffee is too hot that I cannot drink.\", \"The coffee is so hot to drink.\", \"Too hot is the coffee to drink.\"]','The coffee is too hot for me to drink.','\'Too + adjective + for object + to infinitive\'.','\'Too + adjective + for object + to infinitive\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1335,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Change to passive voice: \'The police caught the burglar yesterday.\'','Change to passive voice: \'The police caught the burglar yesterday.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The burglar was caught by the police yesterday.\", \"The burglar is caught by the police yesterday.\", \"The burglar had been caught by the police.\", \"The police was caught by the burglar.\"]','The burglar was caught by the police yesterday.','Simple past passive: \'was caught by\'.','Simple past passive: \'was caught by\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1336,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Choose the correct order of adjectives: \'She bought a _______ dress.\'','Choose the correct order of adjectives: \'She bought a _______ dress.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"beautiful long silk\", \"silk beautiful long\", \"long silk beautiful\", \"beautiful silk long\"]','beautiful long silk','Standard adjective order: Opinion (beautiful) -> Size/Length (long) -> Material (silk).','Standard adjective order: Opinion (beautiful) -> Size/Length (long) -> Material (silk).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1337,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Which sentence contains a correct semicolon (;)?','Which sentence contains a correct semicolon (;)?','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Hafiz loves reading science fiction; his brother prefers playing badminton.\", \"Hafiz loves reading; because his brother plays badminton.\", \"Hafiz loves reading science fiction; and his brother prefers badminton.\", \"Hafiz; loves reading science fiction.\"]','Hafiz loves reading science fiction; his brother prefers playing badminton.','A semicolon joins two related independent clauses without a coordinating conjunction.','A semicolon joins two related independent clauses without a coordinating conjunction.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1338,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Convert to direct speech: \'The teacher told us to open our workbooks.\'','Convert to direct speech: \'The teacher told us to open our workbooks.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"The teacher said, \'Open your workbooks.\'\", \"The teacher said, \'To open your workbooks.\'\", \"The teacher said, \'You open our workbooks.\'\", \"The teacher told, \'Open your workbooks.\'\"]','The teacher said, \'Open your workbooks.\'','Direct imperative with quotation marks.','Direct imperative with quotation marks.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1339,'psr_eng_sentence_structures','psr_english','Combine using \'unless\': \'You will miss the bus if you do not wake up early.\'','Combine using \'unless\': \'You will miss the bus if you do not wake up early.\'','en','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"You will miss the bus unless you wake up early.\", \"Unless you miss the bus you wake up early.\", \"You wake up early unless you will miss the bus.\", \"You will not miss the bus unless you do not wake up early.\"]','You will miss the bus unless you wake up early.','\'Unless\' replaces \'if you do not\'.','\'Unless\' replaces \'if you do not\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1340,'psr_bm_tatabahasa_imbuhan','psr_bahasa_melayu','Pilih ayat yang mengandungi Kata Kerja Transitif:','Pilih ayat yang mengandungi Kata Kerja Transitif:','ms','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Petani itu menanam padi di sawah.\", \"Adik sedang tidur di bilik.\", \"Burung-burung berterbangan di udara.\", \"Bapa tersenyum mendengar berita itu.\"]','Petani itu menanam padi di sawah.','Kata kerja transitif (menanam) memerlukan objek (padi) selepasnya.','Kata kerja transitif (menanam) memerlukan objek (padi) selepasnya.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1341,'psr_bm_tatabahasa_imbuhan','psr_bahasa_melayu','Imbuhan apitan \'ke-...-an\' dalam perkataan \'kejayaan\' membawa maksud:','Imbuhan apitan \'ke-...-an\' dalam perkataan \'kejayaan\' membawa maksud:','ms','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Hal atau keadaan\", \"Saling melakukan\", \"Perbuatan yang disengajakan\", \"Tempat sesuatu berlaku\"]','Hal atau keadaan','Apitan \'ke-...-an\' pada kata dasar \'jaya\' membentuk kata nama abstrak yang bermaksud hal atau keadaan berjaya.','Apitan \'ke-...-an\' pada kata dasar \'jaya\' membentuk kata nama abstrak yang bermaksud hal atau keadaan berjaya.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1342,'psr_bm_tatabahasa_imbuhan','psr_bahasa_melayu','Kanak-kanak itu menangis kerana kakinya _______ duri pokok semalu.','Kanak-kanak itu menangis kerana kakinya _______ duri pokok semalu.','ms','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"tercucuk\", \"mencucuk\", \"dicucukkan\", \"tertusuk\"]','tercucuk','Imbuhan awalan \'ter-\' menunjukkan perbuatan yang tidak disengajakan (tercucuk duri).','Imbuhan awalan \'ter-\' menunjukkan perbuatan yang tidak disengajakan (tercucuk duri).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1343,'psr_bm_tatabahasa_imbuhan','psr_bahasa_melayu','Pilih kata ganda semu yang betul:','Pilih kata ganda semu yang betul:','ms','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"Kanak-kanak\", \"Kura-kura\", \"Gunung-ganang\", \"Kuih-muih\"]','Kura-kura','Kata ganda semu ialah kata yang bentuk dasarnya tidak mempunyai makna jika tidak digandakan (kura-kura, rama-rama, agar-agar).','Kata ganda semu ialah kata yang bentuk dasarnya tidak mempunyai makna jika tidak digandakan (kura-kura, rama-rama, agar-agar).','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"grade\": \"Year 6\"}',0,'Year 6 (PSR)'),(1344,'psr_bm_tatabahasa_imbuhan','psr_bahasa_melayu','Encik Rashid _______ jawatan sebagai pengurus cawangan bank tersebut.','Encik Rashid _______ jawatan sebagai pengurus cawangan bank tersebut.','ms','multiple_choice',NULL,NULL,'[\"menyandang\", \"menyadang\", \"tersandang\", \"disandangkan\"]','menyandang','Ejaan betul dengan imbuhan \'meN-\' pada kata dasar \'sandang\' ialah \'menyandang\'.','Ejaan betul dengan imbuhan \'meN-\' pada kata dasar \'sandang\' ialah \'menyandang\'.','{\"curriculum\": \"Brunei PSR\", \"gr